1
00:00:03,540 --> 00:02:03,540
Visit our website for more: turkision.com

2
00:02:04,040 --> 00:02:07,890
No living being was harmed
during the filming of this series.

3
00:02:09,250 --> 00:02:11,620
Episode 116

4
00:02:30,680 --> 00:02:33,570
Nayman is reborn every day.

5
00:02:34,230 --> 00:02:37,040
Nayman is reborn every day.

6
00:02:40,060 --> 00:02:41,930
Nayman is invincible.

7
00:02:43,240 --> 00:02:46,950
Nayman is invincible and reborn every day.

8
00:02:50,790 --> 00:02:52,810
He is cruel to the enemies.

9
00:02:53,070 --> 00:02:56,120
He is cruel to the enemies.

10
00:02:56,350 --> 00:03:10,360
Nayman.

11
00:04:35,640 --> 00:04:37,190
You.

12
00:04:38,080 --> 00:04:39,670
Prepare the horses.

13
00:04:40,100 --> 00:04:41,470
We'll go.

14
00:04:54,880 --> 00:04:57,840
Nayman must have gone to
headquarters and charged them.

15
00:04:58,710 --> 00:05:00,790
His soldiers must have gone to the tribes.

16
00:05:01,420 --> 00:05:03,470
You said what
you had to say, my Bey.

17
00:05:04,060 --> 00:05:05,880
But the Beys did not listen to you.

18
00:05:06,200 --> 00:05:07,670
They have been besieged.

19
00:05:08,030 --> 00:05:10,640
Being right will not
save the oppressed.

20
00:05:11,380 --> 00:05:15,610
We will all make up for
the mistake that was made.

21
00:05:17,550 --> 00:05:19,620
But Nayman is a smart man.

22
00:05:20,700 --> 00:05:22,820
If he wants to
take the tribes one by one...

23
00:05:23,930 --> 00:05:26,380
He knows very well
that his army will weaken.

24
00:05:27,490 --> 00:05:31,890
For this reason, the Beys
will be required to disband the armies.

25
00:05:32,320 --> 00:05:36,020
Will the Beys disband
their armies, my Bey?

26
00:05:39,780 --> 00:05:41,970
If what we say happens...

27
00:05:43,500 --> 00:05:44,950
That Nayman divides his army...

28
00:05:45,270 --> 00:05:47,850
and spread it around the
tribes to besiege them...

29
00:05:48,560 --> 00:05:53,670
The beys will have no other
way to protect their followers.

30
00:05:54,630 --> 00:05:56,550
My bey, will you permit me to enter?

31
00:05:56,930 --> 00:05:57,980
Come in.

32
00:06:01,950 --> 00:06:04,470
My Bey, Candar is in the north.

33
00:06:04,800 --> 00:06:06,450
Qarasi is in the west.

34
00:06:06,820 --> 00:06:09,090
They've been trapped by Nayman's army.

35
00:06:10,100 --> 00:06:11,800
Beys are helpless.

36
00:06:12,670 --> 00:06:16,610
As for Nayman, he left the
headquarters, my Bey.

37
00:06:19,320 --> 00:06:21,890
So, Nayman might come here.

38
00:06:23,300 --> 00:06:25,030
Send the observers at once.

39
00:06:25,140 --> 00:06:26,490
Come on.

40
00:06:26,510 --> 00:06:27,830
Your command, my Bey.

41
00:06:30,870 --> 00:06:33,180
If he doesn't disband the armies...

42
00:06:34,530 --> 00:06:37,080
he may
want to destroy the tribes then.

43
00:06:37,690 --> 00:06:41,390
Karesi Bey and Candar Bey can't risk this.

44
00:06:41,780 --> 00:06:45,250
We say that his
army numbered 40,000.

45
00:06:47,380 --> 00:06:49,400
Can he be defeated?

46
00:06:49,820 --> 00:06:51,380
It's all over, isn't it?

47
00:06:51,590 --> 00:06:52,550
My Bey.

48
00:06:52,610 --> 00:06:53,940
No.

49
00:06:54,150 --> 00:06:56,030
He will ask for gold.

50
00:06:56,890 --> 00:06:58,950
Then he will give them a deadline.

51
00:07:01,370 --> 00:07:03,910
But Beys are forced to accept this.

52
00:07:07,250 --> 00:07:08,570
Boran.

53
00:07:09,860 --> 00:07:13,190
It doesn't end before we say it.

54
00:07:16,190 --> 00:07:18,680
We will change the
scales on this earth.

55
00:07:20,070 --> 00:07:22,990
We're not giving Nayman an inch of land...

56
00:07:23,630 --> 00:07:25,110
nor any coins.

57
00:07:27,400 --> 00:07:29,400
Start preparations now.

58
00:07:30,180 --> 00:07:31,940
And listen to me well.

59
00:07:33,280 --> 00:07:35,320
Nayman held us accountable...

60
00:07:36,570 --> 00:07:38,280
and set his terms...

61
00:07:38,810 --> 00:07:41,430
and you heard...

62
00:07:41,660 --> 00:07:44,860
What we have heard is not a reason
for us to obey, Mother Sultan.

63
00:07:44,890 --> 00:07:48,110
Nayman appeared before us after
he had campaigned, Yakup Bey.

64
00:07:48,560 --> 00:07:51,460
He said that his
armies are in our land.

65
00:07:51,930 --> 00:07:54,200
They are waiting for a signal from him.

66
00:07:54,290 --> 00:07:56,320
You've heard it.

67
00:07:59,850 --> 00:08:02,470
This is the news coming
from your assistants.

68
00:08:10,080 --> 00:08:12,890
Your people are in great fear.

69
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:17,780
We were caught off guard.

70
00:08:20,800 --> 00:08:24,460
He besieged me here
and attacked my people.

71
00:08:25,340 --> 00:08:27,560
We should have listened to Osman Bey
at the meeting that day.

72
00:08:27,620 --> 00:08:31,060
Remembering what happened
before won't save you now.

73
00:08:31,160 --> 00:08:33,350
Enough of that, Candar Bey.

74
00:08:38,510 --> 00:08:42,490
We will get through
this disaster together.

75
00:08:45,470 --> 00:08:47,780
Since we've been trapped...

76
00:08:52,640 --> 00:08:57,170
So, it's time to put your swords
down and fight with your brains.

77
00:08:59,130 --> 00:09:02,390
Are you saying that there is no
solution but agreement, Mother Sultan?

78
00:09:02,690 --> 00:09:04,300
Unfortunately.

79
00:09:05,690 --> 00:09:08,620
You cannot fight this army alone.

80
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:12,950
And we can't secure Nayman's
orders without you.

81
00:09:16,180 --> 00:09:21,120
We cannot endanger the land of
Candar Bey and Karesi Bey.

82
00:09:21,440 --> 00:09:22,600
We'll agree.

83
00:09:25,090 --> 00:09:28,730
The safety
of my people takes precedence...

84
00:09:29,130 --> 00:09:32,080
but 150 chests of gold...

85
00:09:33,210 --> 00:09:37,520
150, that's too much, Mother Sultan.

86
00:09:38,990 --> 00:09:41,200
Is our strength enough
to do such a thing?

87
00:09:41,250 --> 00:09:43,810
Even if our strength is not
enough to do it, it will happen.

88
00:09:44,010 --> 00:09:45,150
We will make it happen.

89
00:09:47,490 --> 00:09:50,530
If necessary, you will increase
taxes on your people.

90
00:09:51,920 --> 00:09:55,440
They will bear this burden
for their own safety.

91
00:09:58,400 --> 00:10:00,130
Gold can always be found..

92
00:10:00,330 --> 00:10:01,450
...but the soul...

93
00:10:02,800 --> 00:10:05,960
...I'll pay the tax Nayman wants, but...

94
00:10:06,830 --> 00:10:09,750
my people are basically starving.

95
00:10:10,900 --> 00:10:12,810
There must be another way out.

96
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:14,780
Believe me, Karesi Bey...

97
00:10:15,450 --> 00:10:17,470
Cruelty of the Mongols...

98
00:10:17,720 --> 00:10:19,660
is worse than hunger.

99
00:10:21,580 --> 00:10:24,150
Konya will help your people.

100
00:10:25,980 --> 00:10:28,290
Konya will help my people?

101
00:10:28,360 --> 00:10:30,570
Or taxes and horses?

102
00:10:31,540 --> 00:10:33,260
What shall we do, Mother Sultan?

103
00:10:33,560 --> 00:10:34,970
I said what I said.

104
00:10:36,050 --> 00:10:38,730
We'll get out of this press
somehow...

105
00:10:42,530 --> 00:10:48,980
Learn how the tribes of Candar, Karesi and
Germiyanids will be transported the gold.

106
00:10:49,770 --> 00:10:51,360
Your command, my Bey.

107
00:10:52,300 --> 00:10:53,510
Shall we attack?

108
00:10:53,630 --> 00:10:56,370
Yes, we will attack, we will attack.

109
00:10:56,610 --> 00:10:58,790
- Get ready.
- Your command.

110
00:10:59,140 --> 00:11:00,180
Come on!

111
00:11:03,970 --> 00:11:07,210
My Bey, what are we going to do
after we take the gold?

112
00:11:07,940 --> 00:11:10,560
They will raise taxes to get gold...

113
00:11:11,650 --> 00:11:14,500
and taxes will weak people.

114
00:11:15,670 --> 00:11:20,110
We will return the gold to
its wronged owners.

115
00:11:20,210 --> 00:11:21,510
Well, my Bey.

116
00:11:22,430 --> 00:11:24,220
Increase measures.

117
00:11:24,370 --> 00:11:26,530
Put the shooters in high places.

118
00:11:26,640 --> 00:11:27,670
Come on.

119
00:11:27,880 --> 00:11:29,650
Your command.

120
00:11:30,870 --> 00:11:32,140
Gürbüz.

121
00:11:33,830 --> 00:11:36,040
Explode places around the tribe.

122
00:11:36,250 --> 00:11:38,430
Maybe Nayman will set up
a game when he comes over.

123
00:11:38,580 --> 00:11:39,700
Let's be careful.

124
00:11:39,730 --> 00:11:41,180
Your command, my Bey.

125
00:11:47,240 --> 00:11:48,990
May I come in, my Bey?

126
00:11:49,450 --> 00:11:50,970
Come in.

127
00:11:54,630 --> 00:11:56,690
My Bey, there's news
from the observers.

128
00:11:56,810 --> 00:11:58,290
Nayman's coming to the tribe.

129
00:12:01,320 --> 00:12:04,160
Nayman's coming to the tribe, huh?

130
00:12:04,610 --> 00:12:06,120
Let him come.

131
00:12:09,480 --> 00:12:11,560
We are always ready.

132
00:12:13,600 --> 00:12:15,340
The news has reached Konya.

133
00:12:15,360 --> 00:12:18,860
75 Chests of Gold and 5,000 horses...

134
00:12:19,080 --> 00:12:22,120
will be secured from the treasury
of Sultan Aladdin.

135
00:12:22,880 --> 00:12:26,290
And you will secure the rest.

136
00:12:28,010 --> 00:12:29,920
40 chests of gold...

137
00:12:31,750 --> 00:12:33,970
and 3 thousand horses from me.

138
00:12:35,750 --> 00:12:37,550
Mother Sultan says the right thing.

139
00:12:38,060 --> 00:12:39,880
There is no difference between us now.

140
00:12:40,150 --> 00:12:43,450
Karesi Bey, do what you can.

141
00:12:44,610 --> 00:12:49,450
Candar Bey, even If I
search all my tribes...

142
00:12:49,510 --> 00:12:52,180
I can't find 20 chests of gold!

143
00:12:52,450 --> 00:12:54,860
While Yakup Bey provided 40
chests of gold...

144
00:12:54,920 --> 00:12:57,680
how will you present the 15 boxes?

145
00:12:59,520 --> 00:13:00,830
Beys.

146
00:13:01,590 --> 00:13:05,570
Send your messengers at once
and demand gold and horses.

147
00:13:06,930 --> 00:13:09,020
We don't have time to waste

148
00:13:09,030 --> 00:13:10,550
We'll secure it somehow.

149
00:13:11,140 --> 00:13:14,080
Go to your rooms now and think carefully.

150
00:13:14,930 --> 00:13:17,090
If necessary, we will
demand from Beys...

151
00:13:17,100 --> 00:13:21,150
or we will demand a
debt from the Emperor.

152
00:13:21,620 --> 00:13:23,000
But we will have it.

153
00:13:47,800 --> 00:13:49,870
You will be waiting ahead.

154
00:13:50,070 --> 00:13:53,450
You will attack when
the signal comes.

155
00:13:53,890 --> 00:13:58,050
I'll take Frigg and burn the tribe down.

156
00:14:05,690 --> 00:14:07,220
Olof.

157
00:14:07,710 --> 00:14:09,610
There is news from the
observers.

158
00:14:09,660 --> 00:14:11,040
Yes?

159
00:14:11,270 --> 00:14:12,850
Nayman.

160
00:14:13,760 --> 00:14:15,950
Nayman's about to get to the tribe.

161
00:14:16,640 --> 00:14:18,510
Nayman?

162
00:14:22,700 --> 00:14:24,330
What do we do now, Olof?

163
00:14:31,380 --> 00:14:32,790
I told you, Frigg.

164
00:14:32,810 --> 00:14:34,600
The day of reckoning has come.

165
00:14:34,680 --> 00:14:37,210
You will be held
accountable for what you did.

166
00:14:37,880 --> 00:14:39,550
Kill me, kill me.

167
00:14:39,680 --> 00:14:42,060
No, you will not die so easily.

168
00:14:42,740 --> 00:14:44,930
You will first tell us about the
poison you gave Orhan.

169
00:14:44,980 --> 00:14:48,060
Then you'll tell us all the
dirt you've done in detail.

170
00:14:48,650 --> 00:14:49,880
Poison?

171
00:14:54,300 --> 00:14:56,140
I haven't poisoned anyone.

172
00:14:57,790 --> 00:14:58,990
What a liar!

173
00:14:59,020 --> 00:15:01,300
Say it, who made the poison?

174
00:15:01,300 --> 00:15:03,040
Who introduced poison to the tribe?

175
00:15:03,070 --> 00:15:05,070
You will say it all!

176
00:15:06,440 --> 00:15:07,970
Never.

177
00:15:08,900 --> 00:15:10,490
I will never speak.

178
00:15:11,030 --> 00:15:12,840
You can't make me talk, Bala.

179
00:15:12,870 --> 00:15:14,720
You can't force me to speak.

180
00:15:17,920 --> 00:15:20,280
You're going to talk, Frigg.

181
00:15:20,850 --> 00:15:25,720
You will speak and beg for death.

182
00:15:28,750 --> 00:15:29,790
I...

183
00:15:30,360 --> 00:15:32,220
I don't beg to live...

184
00:15:33,030 --> 00:15:34,700
or to die.

185
00:15:38,600 --> 00:15:44,050
But Olof will kill you without
even letting you beg.

186
00:15:44,440 --> 00:15:45,680
He will come here...

187
00:15:46,240 --> 00:15:48,730
and he will destroy you all.

188
00:15:53,260 --> 00:15:55,350
Bala Hatun.
Malhun Hatun.

189
00:15:59,170 --> 00:16:01,780
- What?
- Nayman is coming.

190
00:16:09,970 --> 00:16:11,470
Alps.

191
00:16:11,820 --> 00:16:13,900
Never lose sight of it.

192
00:17:31,380 --> 00:17:32,940
Osman.

193
00:17:33,460 --> 00:17:35,030
Commander Nayman.

194
00:17:45,180 --> 00:17:48,510
Do you know what it means to be
a great person, Osman?

195
00:17:50,050 --> 00:17:54,680
It is for your fame to come
before you come.

196
00:17:54,710 --> 00:17:56,370
Did you hear about my fame?

197
00:17:56,560 --> 00:17:58,330
The hero's bone melts...

198
00:17:59,240 --> 00:18:01,360
but his reputation remains.

199
00:18:10,300 --> 00:18:11,610
You are right.

200
00:18:17,510 --> 00:18:19,240
But it is incomplete.

201
00:18:21,280 --> 00:18:23,920
When everyone who
knows your name dies...

202
00:18:24,270 --> 00:18:25,950
You won't have a reputation either.

203
00:18:26,930 --> 00:18:30,090
I have the power to do this, you know that.

204
00:18:33,780 --> 00:18:35,250
Yes, I know.

205
00:18:36,290 --> 00:18:38,880
But I know something else, too.

206
00:18:39,850 --> 00:18:40,960
Say it.

207
00:18:42,560 --> 00:18:45,980
The end of the arrogant people
has always been defeat.

208
00:18:47,070 --> 00:18:51,830
Of course, look, Mother Sultan and her Beys
are all defeated.

209
00:18:54,660 --> 00:18:58,120
However, I, the great leader, Nayman...

210
00:18:58,970 --> 00:19:02,280
I visit Osman in his tent.

211
00:19:03,610 --> 00:19:05,110
What a great favor!

212
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:17,200
Please ask to prepare
the table for me, Osman.

213
00:19:20,730 --> 00:19:23,700
The guest is always seated in the
best position at the table.

214
00:19:25,390 --> 00:19:26,620
however, say it...

215
00:19:28,440 --> 00:19:30,030
Are you a guest?

216
00:19:31,640 --> 00:19:33,320
Or an enemy?

217
00:19:33,380 --> 00:19:35,920
I'm going to ask
you some questions, Osman.

218
00:19:37,500 --> 00:19:40,690
I will decide after hearing your answers.

219
00:19:58,700 --> 00:20:00,460
Osman.

220
00:20:02,020 --> 00:20:05,320
Olof.

221
00:20:10,020 --> 00:20:11,390
Who is this, Osman?

222
00:20:11,900 --> 00:20:15,050
A dog that will die.

223
00:20:15,250 --> 00:20:17,470
You'll give me Frigg.

224
00:20:17,990 --> 00:20:19,620
If you don't...

225
00:20:20,540 --> 00:20:26,220
I will kill a Muslim for every
hair on her head...

226
00:20:28,020 --> 00:20:31,190
If you hurt one hair of any Muslim...

227
00:20:32,350 --> 00:20:34,720
Then you will pay dearly.

228
00:20:34,870 --> 00:20:36,710
If you don't give me Frigg...

229
00:20:37,050 --> 00:20:40,560
I will spill that blood profusely.

230
00:20:40,770 --> 00:20:42,480
If you want Frigg...

231
00:20:43,420 --> 00:20:46,240
Then you should hand İnegöl over to me.

232
00:20:47,330 --> 00:20:49,970
You are sitting on a
property that is not yours.

233
00:20:50,790 --> 00:20:52,190
Decision is yours.

234
00:20:53,120 --> 00:20:56,330
Either Frigg or İnegöl.

235
00:20:58,150 --> 00:21:00,380
Or I cut off your head
and bury it in İnegöl.

236
00:21:00,430 --> 00:21:01,820
Osman.

237
00:21:10,350 --> 00:21:12,130
I gave orders to my soldiers.

238
00:21:12,490 --> 00:21:14,570
If I am no longer of your tribe...

239
00:21:15,240 --> 00:21:16,850
The massacre will begin.

240
00:21:26,230 --> 00:21:28,060
Marmaracık Castle

241
00:21:28,530 --> 00:21:31,060
Do you hear what you're saying, woman?

242
00:21:31,270 --> 00:21:32,730
What did you do?

243
00:21:32,750 --> 00:21:34,970
How do you drag Frigg
into a trap like that?

244
00:21:35,040 --> 00:21:36,330
Don't worry, Bey.

245
00:21:36,360 --> 00:21:38,070
Frigg will not be caught.

246
00:21:38,160 --> 00:21:39,390
She will not be caught!

247
00:21:39,920 --> 00:21:43,320
How do you know? How do you know?

248
00:21:45,090 --> 00:21:49,320
Did you think of what İsmihan Sultan
would do to us if Frigg was caught?

249
00:21:49,330 --> 00:21:50,830
I know, my Bey!

250
00:21:50,880 --> 00:21:52,460
I thought of everything.

251
00:21:52,840 --> 00:21:55,130
Frigg knows the trap, they
won't catch her.

252
00:21:55,190 --> 00:21:56,750
And I've also said
this several times.

253
00:21:56,780 --> 00:21:59,360
Alçiçek made me do this.
I had no choice.

254
00:21:59,490 --> 00:22:00,770
My Allah!

255
00:22:00,820 --> 00:22:02,260
My Allah!

256
00:22:02,300 --> 00:22:03,590
This isn't good.

257
00:22:03,630 --> 00:22:05,490
This isn't good, Bengi.

258
00:22:05,850 --> 00:22:07,390
This isn't good.

259
00:22:08,480 --> 00:22:10,330
Not only İsmihan Sultan.

260
00:22:10,390 --> 00:22:15,010
What would happen if Bala Hatun found
out that you told her about the trap?

261
00:22:15,650 --> 00:22:17,400
Nothing like this
will happen, Bey.

262
00:22:17,530 --> 00:22:21,030
My Allah!

263
00:22:21,140 --> 00:22:22,690
May I come in?

264
00:22:22,730 --> 00:22:24,570
Come in, my daughter.

265
00:22:31,900 --> 00:22:33,050
Mother.

266
00:22:34,150 --> 00:22:35,970
Ayşe Hatun sent a message.

267
00:22:37,470 --> 00:22:38,560
Frigg.

268
00:22:41,590 --> 00:22:42,980
They caught Frigg.

269
00:22:48,300 --> 00:22:51,000
This is good news, very nice news.

270
00:22:53,190 --> 00:22:55,500
Come on, my daughter, mind
your business.

271
00:23:06,780 --> 00:23:12,030
Say, what are we going to do now?

272
00:23:23,100 --> 00:23:26,220
Olof wrote me a letter.

273
00:23:27,060 --> 00:23:28,980
He showed his devotion to me.

274
00:23:30,660 --> 00:23:33,570
For this reason, he is
under my protection.

275
00:23:34,500 --> 00:23:36,200
You won't touch him.

276
00:23:46,710 --> 00:23:49,360
Only I pass judgment in Kayı tribe.

277
00:23:52,430 --> 00:23:55,150
Of course, if you are willing to
pay the price.

278
00:23:59,370 --> 00:24:01,180
As for you, Olof...

279
00:24:02,600 --> 00:24:04,780
You will not carry out a
massacre in İnegöl.

280
00:24:04,890 --> 00:24:07,150
Frigg and İnegöl are mine.

281
00:24:07,590 --> 00:24:10,460
If Osman makes a mistake...

282
00:24:15,610 --> 00:24:17,500
Big talk.

283
00:24:18,290 --> 00:24:20,150
You are very brave.

284
00:24:23,250 --> 00:24:24,760
I love the brave.

285
00:24:26,260 --> 00:24:30,350
But my love does not prevent my anger.

286
00:24:31,320 --> 00:24:34,840
Sit in your castle now, Olof...

287
00:24:37,020 --> 00:24:38,880
and think of Osman's offer.

288
00:24:41,860 --> 00:24:43,410
Osman.

289
00:24:45,000 --> 00:24:46,890
I will come for you.

290
00:24:48,260 --> 00:24:50,090
This will be the last time you come.

291
00:25:13,850 --> 00:25:16,400
The table, Osman, the table.

292
00:25:35,100 --> 00:25:36,660
Olof!

293
00:25:36,890 --> 00:25:38,380
Olof!

294
00:25:38,470 --> 00:25:39,840
Shut up.

295
00:25:39,940 --> 00:25:41,260
Shut up.

296
00:25:42,050 --> 00:25:43,970
Olof, whom you
trust so much, is gone.

297
00:25:44,030 --> 00:25:46,080
Olof is gone, but you stayed here.

298
00:25:47,110 --> 00:25:48,950
You can't escape from my hands.

299
00:25:49,330 --> 00:25:52,710
If you want to survive, you will
answer my questions first.

300
00:26:00,860 --> 00:26:03,210
Your questions will remain unanswered.

301
00:26:04,520 --> 00:26:09,560
I go to the grave with my secrets.

302
00:26:09,880 --> 00:26:11,530
You're going to talk, Frigg.

303
00:26:12,540 --> 00:26:14,070
You collaborated with İsmihan.

304
00:26:14,100 --> 00:26:15,970
And the infection was
transmitted to the people

305
00:26:16,000 --> 00:26:17,700
And what about
my dear Orhan?

306
00:26:17,850 --> 00:26:19,130
You poisoned him.

307
00:26:19,210 --> 00:26:20,410
You will tell us about
the antidote.

308
00:26:20,430 --> 00:26:24,230
And whoever brought
it into the tribe, you'll say it all.

309
00:26:29,590 --> 00:26:33,090
You can never know.

310
00:26:33,950 --> 00:26:41,140
If I die, Orhan will go to
the grave alive.

311
00:26:41,680 --> 00:26:42,820
Shut up.

312
00:26:44,580 --> 00:26:46,080
Just tell me.

313
00:26:48,830 --> 00:26:50,340
Orhan.

314
00:26:53,360 --> 00:26:56,210
The poison had circulated in
his body a long time ago.

315
00:26:57,170 --> 00:26:59,460
He has little time left

316
00:26:59,970 --> 00:27:01,820
A very short time later...

317
00:27:02,460 --> 00:27:04,840
His recovery will be impossible.

318
00:27:05,800 --> 00:27:08,730
His body will become as hard as stone.

319
00:27:12,320 --> 00:27:15,000
He will not be able to return
to his former self.

320
00:27:18,440 --> 00:27:22,600
We'll see how much time you have left.

321
00:27:28,340 --> 00:27:31,070
Yenişehir

322
00:27:37,840 --> 00:27:39,910
Would you permit me, Mother Sultan?

323
00:27:41,900 --> 00:27:44,040
Come in, Bayındır.

324
00:27:51,230 --> 00:27:54,320
I have bad news, Mother Sultan.

325
00:27:55,420 --> 00:27:56,850
Frigg...

326
00:27:57,180 --> 00:27:58,740
What happened to Frigg?

327
00:28:00,250 --> 00:28:03,480
Bala Hatun has captured Frigg Hatun.

328
00:28:04,230 --> 00:28:06,730
She is now a prisoner of the Kayı tribe.

329
00:28:07,010 --> 00:28:08,770
Frigg won't talk.

330
00:28:10,520 --> 00:28:12,380
If she opens her mouth...

331
00:28:13,260 --> 00:28:15,920
You're going to shut it down, Bayındır.

332
00:28:17,780 --> 00:28:21,390
Mother Sultan, what are we going to do?

333
00:28:21,920 --> 00:28:22,960
That place is the Kayı tribe.

334
00:28:23,000 --> 00:28:26,790
You can't get in, and if you get in, you
can never get out.

335
00:28:27,840 --> 00:28:29,430
Olof won't stand still either.

336
00:28:29,520 --> 00:28:31,090
You're will go in, Bayındır.

337
00:28:31,590 --> 00:28:34,610
Do whatever you have to do and get Frigg
out of there.

338
00:28:36,240 --> 00:28:38,430
You won't be alone, however...

339
00:28:39,800 --> 00:28:44,970
What Frigg says matters to
Bengi Hatun too.

340
00:28:45,660 --> 00:28:47,800
We will solve this.

341
00:28:50,320 --> 00:28:52,840
Will you let me in, Mother Sultan?

342
00:28:53,430 --> 00:28:54,910
Come in, Celali.

343
00:28:57,380 --> 00:28:58,570
Mother Sultan.

344
00:28:58,680 --> 00:28:59,900
Nayman.

345
00:29:00,260 --> 00:29:02,390
He arrived at the Kayı tribe.

346
00:29:14,480 --> 00:29:17,030
What you ate and what you
drank, let it be yours.

347
00:29:19,100 --> 00:29:21,750
But tell us why you came here.

348
00:29:22,790 --> 00:29:25,900
Stop, let me drink my Ayran.

349
00:29:41,350 --> 00:29:44,670
Ayran is very tasty!

350
00:29:45,290 --> 00:29:47,790
This is the best I have ever had.

351
00:29:50,170 --> 00:29:51,870
Enjoy it.

352
00:29:57,200 --> 00:29:59,620
People ride horses...

353
00:30:00,470 --> 00:30:04,310
they get hungry, they
drink and they fight.

354
00:30:05,160 --> 00:30:09,620
Then, they have the best gifts.

355
00:30:09,970 --> 00:30:11,070
Isn't it, Osman?

356
00:30:19,380 --> 00:30:21,840
But I heard...

357
00:30:22,340 --> 00:30:25,470
that God withdrew
these gifts from your son.

358
00:30:25,750 --> 00:30:29,070
He can't
ride a horse or draw a sword.

359
00:30:32,920 --> 00:30:35,690
He can't even eat his own food.

360
00:30:36,650 --> 00:30:38,710
He who knows the pain
of a wound best...

361
00:30:39,890 --> 00:30:41,760
is who caused it.

362
00:30:45,420 --> 00:30:47,980
If you are related to this...

363
00:30:48,820 --> 00:30:51,090
Or the one who was stabbed
and wounded a lot.

364
00:30:52,830 --> 00:30:56,400
I have a lot of soldiers
who have been in this situation.

365
00:30:57,880 --> 00:31:00,160
They were hit with poisoned arrows.

366
00:31:01,120 --> 00:31:05,250
I have no business with
these little games, Osman.

367
00:31:05,420 --> 00:31:10,340
Also, didn't you arrest Olof's
wife, Frigg, for this reason?

368
00:31:11,500 --> 00:31:14,120
I will not get involved in your problems.

369
00:31:21,200 --> 00:31:23,140
You know a lot.

370
00:31:25,320 --> 00:31:27,130
Information is the source of power.

371
00:31:27,180 --> 00:31:30,660
Where is your son now?

372
00:31:31,130 --> 00:31:32,780
He is having treatment.

373
00:31:33,100 --> 00:31:35,290
It will last forever.

374
00:31:35,890 --> 00:31:37,840
They said he was petrified.

375
00:31:40,750 --> 00:31:44,280
You want to see him
walk again, right?

376
00:31:46,860 --> 00:31:49,110
He will walk, Inshallah.

377
00:31:51,420 --> 00:31:53,370
He will recover and rise.

378
00:31:55,960 --> 00:32:01,220
Then I will grant your wish, Osman.

379
00:32:04,230 --> 00:32:07,330
I can cure Orhan.

380
00:32:12,370 --> 00:32:14,080
Shaman.

381
00:32:38,500 --> 00:32:41,090
My Allah.

382
00:32:41,910 --> 00:32:43,460
You will recover, son.

383
00:32:43,560 --> 00:32:45,450
The mother's heart feels that.

384
00:32:45,930 --> 00:32:47,500
You will be fine.

385
00:32:49,080 --> 00:32:50,390
Mother.

386
00:32:51,360 --> 00:32:53,210
What's going on inside?

387
00:32:56,100 --> 00:32:57,980
Nothing happens, son.

388
00:33:04,750 --> 00:33:06,290
Osman.

389
00:33:07,640 --> 00:33:09,390
Come on, let's see, son.

390
00:33:13,150 --> 00:33:14,960
Where are we going, father?

391
00:33:15,300 --> 00:33:17,160
We're going to see Nayman's doctor.

392
00:33:19,410 --> 00:33:20,690
Nayman?

393
00:33:22,590 --> 00:33:23,970
Osman.

394
00:33:26,900 --> 00:33:28,050
Come on.

395
00:33:31,250 --> 00:33:34,770
Can this man be trusted, Osman?
What if he did something?

396
00:33:34,850 --> 00:33:36,410
We tried everything, Malhun.

397
00:33:37,260 --> 00:33:38,470
Don't worry.

398
00:33:38,600 --> 00:33:40,830
He can't do anything, we're all there.

399
00:33:42,530 --> 00:33:44,990
Kumral Abdal
will check it out first

400
00:33:47,810 --> 00:33:49,680
Are you sure, dear Osman?

401
00:33:49,730 --> 00:33:51,250
The world is like this, Malhun.

402
00:33:52,190 --> 00:33:53,930
You can take advantage of the enemy.

403
00:33:54,070 --> 00:33:56,100
and harm from a friend.

404
00:34:16,679 --> 00:34:18,469
Your breath is counted, Frigg.

405
00:34:18,840 --> 00:34:20,860
But if you insist on being stubborn...

406
00:34:21,159 --> 00:34:22,690
I will be stubborn too.

407
00:34:37,780 --> 00:34:40,649
You will talk and Orhan will survive.

408
00:34:42,050 --> 00:34:44,969
I can only be patient for
Orhan's health, Frigg.

409
00:34:46,520 --> 00:34:47,520
Bala.

410
00:34:49,350 --> 00:34:50,710
Orhan.

411
00:34:52,100 --> 00:34:55,780
He will never be able to
get back on his feet.

412
00:34:56,228 --> 00:34:58,400
You didn't hit your target, Frigg.

413
00:35:00,040 --> 00:35:01,140
Bala.

414
00:35:02,780 --> 00:35:04,200
We found the antidote.

415
00:35:06,020 --> 00:35:07,440
Thank Allah.

416
00:35:16,380 --> 00:35:18,580
Now you think about the rest, Frigg.

417
00:35:18,630 --> 00:35:20,630
You have nothing more to give us.

418
00:35:20,860 --> 00:35:22,300
Death awaits you.

419
00:35:24,640 --> 00:35:28,590
Now who's going to take
you from my arms, Frigg?

420
00:35:45,400 --> 00:35:46,540
Osman.

421
00:36:51,630 --> 00:36:52,630
Wait.

422
00:36:58,020 --> 00:36:59,220
His condition is bad.

423
00:37:08,680 --> 00:37:12,000
The poison had spread
throughout his body.

424
00:37:13,390 --> 00:37:15,240
When his limbs are petrified...

425
00:37:15,690 --> 00:37:18,210
and the blood flow stops the body...

426
00:37:18,470 --> 00:37:20,230
he loses his strength.

427
00:37:20,640 --> 00:37:22,160
There is one solution.

428
00:37:23,050 --> 00:37:24,610
Say, what is it?

429
00:37:26,400 --> 00:37:27,720
Say it.

430
00:37:28,180 --> 00:37:31,030
Hot water.

431
00:37:32,040 --> 00:37:33,560
Come on, Malhun.

432
00:37:47,690 --> 00:37:49,250
Boran.

433
00:37:49,640 --> 00:37:51,440
Summon Kumral Abdal.

434
00:37:51,840 --> 00:37:53,430
Your command, my Bey.

435
00:37:53,670 --> 00:37:55,050
Ayaz.

436
00:39:23,600 --> 00:39:24,960
No.

437
00:39:26,080 --> 00:39:28,410
My doctor will look at it first.

438
00:39:34,080 --> 00:39:36,000
A misplaced precaution, Osman.

439
00:39:36,440 --> 00:39:38,730
What could happen to your son
more than that?

440
00:39:44,700 --> 00:39:46,280
You can help me.

441
00:39:46,900 --> 00:39:48,530
And you can't help me.

442
00:39:49,480 --> 00:39:52,010
Orhan will rise to
his feet anyway.

443
00:39:53,070 --> 00:39:55,300
But what you call a precaution...

444
00:39:56,280 --> 00:39:58,430
is Kumral Abdal who keeps us going.

445
00:40:03,660 --> 00:40:04,970
May I, my Bey?

446
00:40:04,970 --> 00:40:06,600
Come in, Kumral Abdal.

447
00:40:11,560 --> 00:40:12,700
My Bey.

448
00:40:17,630 --> 00:40:18,840
Kumral Abdal.

449
00:40:20,810 --> 00:40:22,390
Look at this.

450
00:40:22,680 --> 00:40:25,010
It's the medicine he
prepared for Orhan's treatment.

451
00:40:25,040 --> 00:40:26,420
Look at it.

452
00:40:36,470 --> 00:40:38,020
You.

453
00:41:11,000 --> 00:41:12,710
The herb that will give healing...

454
00:41:13,450 --> 00:41:16,260
expresses itself with its
taste after its smell.

455
00:41:19,340 --> 00:41:20,590
It is not known.

456
00:41:21,690 --> 00:41:23,460
I don't know if it will help.

457
00:41:23,930 --> 00:41:26,810
But it is not harmful.

458
00:41:33,660 --> 00:41:35,400
Are you sure, Kumral Abdal?

459
00:41:36,960 --> 00:41:39,160
I don't know if it is cured.

460
00:41:40,070 --> 00:41:41,260
But it is not harmful.

461
00:41:44,420 --> 00:41:49,120
It keeps those who are
badly wounded in war on their feet...

462
00:41:49,790 --> 00:41:52,670
and those who fall to the
ground with poison as well.

463
00:41:55,600 --> 00:41:57,070
Trust me, Osman.

464
00:42:18,000 --> 00:42:19,310
Give him.

465
00:42:24,640 --> 00:42:28,410
In the name of Allah, the most
gracious, the most merciful.

466
00:42:30,610 --> 00:42:31,820
O healer.

467
00:42:38,910 --> 00:42:42,940
In the name of Allah, the most
gracious, the most merciful.

468
00:42:47,940 --> 00:42:49,930
O healer.

469
00:42:52,110 --> 00:42:54,120
O healer.

470
00:43:43,510 --> 00:43:45,240
Where are the rest of these herbs?

471
00:43:46,160 --> 00:43:49,570
I mean, if it's going to work, it
has to be boiled every day.

472
00:43:52,290 --> 00:43:57,170
Since Nayman came here alone
as a guest without his army...

473
00:44:00,600 --> 00:44:02,510
He must give us the rest.

474
00:44:04,860 --> 00:44:06,380
You.

475
00:44:27,470 --> 00:44:28,850
Come on.

476
00:44:28,880 --> 00:44:30,890
Take Orhan inside to rest.

477
00:44:46,480 --> 00:44:48,900
You didn't come here to help my son.

478
00:44:52,560 --> 00:44:54,940
Say what is the reason
for your coming.

479
00:45:16,660 --> 00:45:18,420
Aren't they crowded, my Bey?

480
00:45:18,590 --> 00:45:21,490
Yes, they are.

481
00:45:23,240 --> 00:45:25,650
But there is nothing
difficult for us, Acar.

482
00:45:26,980 --> 00:45:31,100
When this caravan reaches
Olof, he will have more strength.

483
00:45:33,340 --> 00:45:35,290
Things will get worse then.

484
00:45:36,450 --> 00:45:39,180
But we are here not to allow that.

485
00:45:39,620 --> 00:45:44,350
We're here to cut off that
hand when the time comes.

486
00:45:57,990 --> 00:45:59,380
Now!

487
00:46:01,280 --> 00:46:02,630
Turks!

488
00:46:03,090 --> 00:46:05,300
The field is now ours, Alps!

489
00:46:05,640 --> 00:46:07,020
Come on!

490
00:46:08,040 --> 00:46:09,540
O Allah!

491
00:46:47,800 --> 00:46:50,920
Mother Sultan and the Beys
have surrendered.

492
00:46:53,960 --> 00:46:55,730
There is no war anymore.

493
00:46:56,440 --> 00:46:58,230
Let's say I started an attack...

494
00:46:59,500 --> 00:47:01,620
How would you
defend your lands?

495
00:47:01,950 --> 00:47:04,280
Tell me, let's see, Osman.

496
00:47:39,810 --> 00:47:41,890
Divide your army into four legions.

497
00:47:43,940 --> 00:47:45,450
First legion...

498
00:47:47,630 --> 00:47:49,470
is standing behind Candar Bey.

499
00:47:53,480 --> 00:47:54,580
The second...

500
00:47:56,170 --> 00:47:58,160
walks towards Karesi Bey.

501
00:47:59,600 --> 00:48:00,900
And...

502
00:48:03,510 --> 00:48:04,820
the third...

503
00:48:09,790 --> 00:48:11,860
the army which you are leading...

504
00:48:15,950 --> 00:48:17,320
it...

505
00:48:19,540 --> 00:48:22,610
stands facing Mother
Sultan's headquarters.

506
00:48:27,210 --> 00:48:28,770
You said four.

507
00:48:29,230 --> 00:48:30,550
You counted three, Osman.

508
00:48:33,410 --> 00:48:34,570
The fourth legion...

509
00:48:37,870 --> 00:48:39,270
is the one you hid.

510
00:48:41,280 --> 00:48:44,780
There it is, it's standing here.

511
00:48:50,570 --> 00:48:52,650
When Beys attack you...

512
00:48:54,340 --> 00:48:58,980
you will return with
10,000 of your soldiers...

513
00:49:01,440 --> 00:49:04,440
and come to where t
his fourth unit is.

514
00:49:05,880 --> 00:49:08,060
And you will kill the Beys like this.

515
00:49:09,520 --> 00:49:11,610
I thought you knew the Three Legions.

516
00:49:12,190 --> 00:49:16,820
But you knew about the legion that was
going to attack from the rear as well.

517
00:49:20,210 --> 00:49:23,030
Fortunately, there is no
need for this anymore.

518
00:49:23,770 --> 00:49:26,340
Beys will bring me gold.

519
00:49:27,130 --> 00:49:28,810
What about you?

520
00:49:29,260 --> 00:49:32,600
You wanted to be at the head of
the army that was established.

521
00:49:33,130 --> 00:49:36,120
If you were at the lead, what
would you do?

522
00:49:41,910 --> 00:49:44,480
You only trust the number
of your soldiers.

523
00:49:47,050 --> 00:49:48,700
But this place is our home.

524
00:49:51,340 --> 00:49:58,510
We know the straits and rivers
that will stop your army.

525
00:50:24,910 --> 00:50:26,490
You're going to Olof...

526
00:50:26,750 --> 00:50:28,300
but tell him...

527
00:50:28,820 --> 00:50:34,150
that his punishment
in these lands is death.

528
00:50:35,680 --> 00:50:37,010
Did you hear me?

529
00:50:38,950 --> 00:50:40,780
Go now before I kill you.

530
00:50:58,040 --> 00:51:01,190
Collect the gold, chariots and
everything that is there, valiants.

531
00:51:01,390 --> 00:51:02,700
We will return to the tribe.

532
00:51:03,210 --> 00:51:04,210
Victory is ours!

533
00:51:04,240 --> 00:51:07,640
Allah is great!
Allah is great!

534
00:51:08,080 --> 00:51:10,160
For the campaign I'm going to do...

535
00:51:18,730 --> 00:51:19,840
I can say it.

536
00:51:22,310 --> 00:51:27,040
You were going to divide the army
into a hundred sections...

537
00:51:27,430 --> 00:51:31,010
and try to drain my soldiers.

538
00:51:31,840 --> 00:51:34,640
But the thing you
overlooked, Osman, is...

539
00:51:36,570 --> 00:51:38,660
You still think of yourself
as someone from the tribe.

540
00:51:38,900 --> 00:51:43,560
You will lose your cities and
locations when you withdraw inside.

541
00:51:44,170 --> 00:51:46,340
Quitting would have finished you off.

542
00:51:54,580 --> 00:52:00,740
I wasn't going to do anything you said.

543
00:52:03,560 --> 00:52:05,830
If you want to see what I do...

544
00:52:06,820 --> 00:52:08,520
You should test it then.

545
00:52:12,210 --> 00:52:13,540
However...

546
00:52:15,540 --> 00:52:18,590
My campaigns are kept secret until then.

547
00:52:28,310 --> 00:52:29,680
My Bey.

548
00:52:35,740 --> 00:52:37,310
Kumral Abdal.

549
00:52:39,010 --> 00:52:41,630
Orhan Bey started to feel
numbness in his feet.

550
00:52:45,490 --> 00:52:48,430
The effect of the poison
is starting to stop, thank Allah.

551
00:52:50,140 --> 00:52:51,910
What are you saying?

552
00:53:11,650 --> 00:53:13,490
Thank Allah.

553
00:53:18,550 --> 00:53:20,110
Thank Allah.

554
00:53:44,910 --> 00:53:46,290
Thank you.

555
00:53:57,130 --> 00:53:58,960
Thank you, Commander Nayman.

556
00:54:00,890 --> 00:54:05,210
Killing a soul and
making it heal is a skill.

557
00:54:07,430 --> 00:54:09,470
We have both, Osman.

558
00:54:18,160 --> 00:54:19,350
I want to host you.

559
00:54:20,630 --> 00:54:22,110
You are my guest for tonight.

560
00:54:24,630 --> 00:54:29,230
I am a heavy
guest, Osman, can you host me?

561
00:54:30,790 --> 00:54:32,110
Boran.

562
00:54:32,410 --> 00:54:33,760
My Bey.

563
00:54:34,060 --> 00:54:38,000
Make the best tent and the best bed.

564
00:54:41,420 --> 00:54:43,180
Commander will stay with us.

565
00:54:44,550 --> 00:54:46,300
Your command, my Bey.

566
00:55:12,060 --> 00:55:13,610
Orhan.

567
00:55:19,790 --> 00:55:21,090
Father.

568
00:55:21,150 --> 00:55:22,690
Orhan.

569
00:55:24,970 --> 00:55:26,790
I feel my legs, father.

570
00:55:27,940 --> 00:55:29,740
Thank Allah.

571
00:55:30,550 --> 00:55:33,700
Thank Allah.
Come here.

572
00:55:33,800 --> 00:55:34,830
Come here.

573
00:55:35,720 --> 00:55:38,920
Mashallah.

574
00:55:38,930 --> 00:55:41,820
Thank Allah, my dear Osman.

575
00:55:42,030 --> 00:55:43,570
Kumral Abdal.

576
00:55:43,910 --> 00:55:45,690
What's the situation?

577
00:55:45,740 --> 00:55:47,590
The medicine is effective, Osman Bey.

578
00:55:48,150 --> 00:55:49,730
He feels his legs now.

579
00:55:50,530 --> 00:55:53,120
The poison will lose its effect
little by little, Inshallah.

580
00:55:53,160 --> 00:55:55,280
- Inshallah.
- My Orhan.

581
00:55:55,410 --> 00:55:57,450
When will I get back on
my feet, Kumral Abdal?

582
00:55:57,500 --> 00:55:59,590
Let the poison lose its effect first.

583
00:56:00,360 --> 00:56:02,880
you will stand up, Inshallah, my Bey.

584
00:56:04,100 --> 00:56:07,660
He will, my son will return to
his former self.

585
00:56:09,420 --> 00:56:10,660
Inshallah.

586
00:56:10,700 --> 00:56:14,260
Son, you have passed another exam.

587
00:56:15,200 --> 00:56:18,810
Mashallah, your heart is as
strong as your wrist.

588
00:56:19,410 --> 00:56:21,700
Come on, come on, lie down like this.

589
00:56:22,360 --> 00:56:24,230
Come on, lie down like this

590
00:56:35,770 --> 00:56:37,340
Osman.

591
00:56:38,980 --> 00:56:40,830
Why did Nayman give us the antidote?

592
00:56:47,760 --> 00:56:49,800
I had told you before too.

593
00:56:50,030 --> 00:56:52,740
We've never seen an
enemy like this before.

594
00:56:58,290 --> 00:57:00,860
Can there be an enemy who
keeps our son on his feet?

595
00:57:03,080 --> 00:57:04,660
Yes.

596
00:57:05,390 --> 00:57:07,050
Nayman's intention is...

597
00:57:07,900 --> 00:57:11,210
to leave us defenseless
before it overcomes us.

598
00:57:12,790 --> 00:57:14,890
He makes our hearts
feel warm towards him...

599
00:57:15,320 --> 00:57:18,010
and wants to
put us under his command after that.

600
00:57:22,500 --> 00:57:24,160
Well, what are you going to do?

601
00:57:24,380 --> 00:57:26,800
I'll give him a
corresponding answer, Malhun.

602
00:57:27,080 --> 00:57:28,600
Don't worry.

603
00:57:29,070 --> 00:57:30,760
He wants to hit us
in our hearts.

604
00:57:33,620 --> 00:57:35,700
We will soften his heart.

605
00:57:38,320 --> 00:57:39,620
Kumral.

606
00:57:40,770 --> 00:57:44,560
Tell Alps to invite my Sheikh
to dinner in the evening.

607
00:57:52,050 --> 00:57:54,860
And we will invite Nayman to Islam.

608
00:58:00,370 --> 00:58:01,600
If it happens...

609
00:58:01,960 --> 00:58:05,350
We will win a heart
this time, not a war.

610
00:58:08,170 --> 00:58:09,300
What if not?

611
00:58:11,120 --> 00:58:13,350
If this is not done, then the path
we will follow is known.

612
00:58:13,440 --> 00:58:14,690
It is the way of war.

613
00:58:16,730 --> 00:58:22,980
But I would like him to
live with us who came to kill us.

614
00:58:29,390 --> 00:58:31,060
İnegöl Castle

615
00:58:32,090 --> 00:58:34,810
Since Olof didn't find whoever
blew up the armory...

616
00:58:35,100 --> 00:58:37,160
he must increase the measures taken.

617
00:58:40,210 --> 00:58:42,000
You have to help us.

618
00:58:42,020 --> 00:58:44,080
We have to get closer to Olof.

619
00:58:46,150 --> 00:58:50,110
He asked for your help in getting Frigg
to convert to Christianity, didn't he?

620
00:58:50,130 --> 00:58:51,480
Yes.

621
00:58:51,890 --> 00:58:55,390
But Frigg must have fallen into Bala
Hatun's hands a long time ago.

622
00:58:56,090 --> 00:58:58,740
By now she must have paid
for everything she did.

623
00:58:59,170 --> 00:59:01,590
He will need you more now.

624
00:59:02,490 --> 00:59:05,140
And he'll ask you to
pray for Frigg.

625
00:59:05,950 --> 00:59:07,320
We can exploit this.

626
00:59:09,080 --> 00:59:11,010
I don't like it.

627
00:59:15,550 --> 00:59:16,920
Did I say that out loud?

628
00:59:22,580 --> 00:59:24,940
I mean... I wanted to say...

629
00:59:29,400 --> 00:59:31,460
Be careful, Ülgen Hatun.

630
00:59:32,930 --> 00:59:35,760
My Bey wanted me to take care
of you, that's why I said so.

631
00:59:35,840 --> 00:59:38,160
Yes, Cerkutay, yes,
I get you, yes.

632
00:59:41,920 --> 00:59:43,480
As you understand, come on.

633
00:59:44,180 --> 00:59:45,590
Come on, come on, let's go.

634
00:59:58,550 --> 01:00:01,390
May the great Jesus protect us!
What happened?

635
01:00:02,980 --> 01:00:04,540
Olof!

636
01:00:07,480 --> 01:00:09,210
What happened?

637
01:00:09,890 --> 01:00:11,950
Turgut attacked us.

638
01:00:17,130 --> 01:00:19,930
Where's the gold and soldiers?

639
01:00:20,290 --> 01:00:22,150
He left no one alive.

640
01:00:22,260 --> 01:00:23,780
And he took the gold.

641
01:00:24,160 --> 01:00:25,970
He said he would come for you.

642
01:00:28,830 --> 01:00:30,350
Osman!

643
01:00:31,030 --> 01:00:32,800
Turgut!

644
01:00:34,370 --> 01:00:36,720
You will pay very dearly for this.

645
01:00:37,330 --> 01:00:39,570
I will separate your bones from your skin.

646
01:00:45,700 --> 01:00:50,970
Their bloodshed is more important than
worship in the church, Commander Olof.

647
01:00:52,000 --> 01:00:54,700
We'll take revenge on those
who stole our gold.

648
01:00:56,500 --> 01:00:58,030
Don't worry.

649
01:00:59,080 --> 01:01:00,270
Sister Irene.

650
01:01:03,490 --> 01:01:05,600
Soldier, come with me.

651
01:01:16,560 --> 01:01:19,110
Marmaracık Castle

652
01:01:24,180 --> 01:01:25,510
Stop now, my Bey.

653
01:01:25,570 --> 01:01:26,620
Stop now.

654
01:01:26,890 --> 01:01:28,420
Should I?

655
01:01:30,160 --> 01:01:34,150
The situation is very bad.

656
01:01:34,510 --> 01:01:37,480
If Frigg talks, Osman will attack us.

657
01:01:39,410 --> 01:01:45,400
Then, there will be no more kinship or
council, or Aktemur and Alçiçek.

658
01:01:48,600 --> 01:01:51,620
We could even lose our lives
because of what you did.

659
01:01:52,280 --> 01:01:56,540
Do you think that when Mother Sultan learns of the matter, will she remain silent about that situation?

660
01:01:56,620 --> 01:01:59,640
I know this, tell me
something I don't know.

661
01:02:00,990 --> 01:02:04,050
I'll go and talk to Mother Sultan
when she finds out the matter.

662
01:02:04,090 --> 01:02:07,310
What are you going to tell her?
What are you going to say?

663
01:02:08,860 --> 01:02:11,660
Are you going to tell her that you
set Frigg up?

664
01:02:15,980 --> 01:02:19,530
Will Mother Sultan keep you
alive afterwards, woman?

665
01:02:25,360 --> 01:02:28,930
Mother Sultan could not
simply kill me like this.

666
01:02:29,790 --> 01:02:32,790
I also know what Frigg knows, or do
you think I wouldn't talk if she did?

667
01:02:32,840 --> 01:02:37,300
Of course you will.
You don't even shut up.

668
01:02:40,730 --> 01:02:42,540
Alps!

669
01:02:46,300 --> 01:02:47,650
Did you do what
I told you to do?

670
01:02:47,680 --> 01:02:51,330
The wagons of supplies have come to the
castle now and the weapons are on their way.

671
01:02:51,520 --> 01:02:53,320
Alps that you requested are
coming from the tribe.

672
01:02:53,510 --> 01:02:56,280
Well, be careful.

673
01:02:59,810 --> 01:03:01,170
What's happening, Bey?

674
01:03:02,910 --> 01:03:04,670
Why all these preparations?

675
01:03:09,370 --> 01:03:15,340
You think you're smart and you're telling
me you will talk if Frigg does.

676
01:03:16,600 --> 01:03:23,250
Mother Sulta will try to kill
you so you won't speak.

677
01:03:24,020 --> 01:03:25,720
Do you understand now?

678
01:03:35,480 --> 01:03:39,240
But it's over.

679
01:03:40,170 --> 01:03:43,450
It's over, it's over now, Hatun.

680
01:03:46,370 --> 01:03:49,880
Marmaracık will become an
impenetrable fortress.

681
01:03:50,990 --> 01:03:53,140
Yenişehir

682
01:03:54,010 --> 01:03:55,970
When will these gold
coins come?

683
01:03:56,010 --> 01:03:59,610
My children are trying to collect them
as best as they can, Mother Sultan.

684
01:04:00,000 --> 01:04:02,160
But, no.

685
01:04:03,590 --> 01:04:07,600
We were talking about 15 chests, but
if we collect five of them, we'll be done.

686
01:04:09,790 --> 01:04:12,550
The same situation exists
for us, Mother Sultan.

687
01:04:13,060 --> 01:04:16,750
The sons are trying to collect everything.

688
01:04:16,890 --> 01:04:21,440
But we're a long way from the
amount we need to collect.

689
01:04:24,770 --> 01:04:26,040
What about you, Takup Bey?

690
01:04:26,420 --> 01:04:28,340
We collect gold coins.

691
01:04:28,870 --> 01:04:34,730
But we won't be able to collect all
of them in this short time.

692
01:04:37,800 --> 01:04:40,080
What shall we do now, Mother Sultan?

693
01:04:41,600 --> 01:04:46,530
When Nayman sees we've raised
less money for him than he asked for...

694
01:04:46,840 --> 01:04:49,490
he won't show any understanding.

695
01:04:51,450 --> 01:04:54,330
Even if we give him everything we have...

696
01:04:55,230 --> 01:04:58,030
we won't be able to provide him with
the quantity he asked for.

697
01:04:58,070 --> 01:05:01,750
Where will we find all this amount
of gold money, Mother Sultan?

698
01:05:05,695 --> 01:05:10,565
We have no other solution than to collect
the entire amount of gold Nayman requested

699
01:05:15,435 --> 01:05:19,775
For this reason, we will call help
from Osman Bey if we have to.

700
01:05:27,015 --> 01:05:31,235
I have brought you greetings
from Mother Sultan.

701
01:05:32,305 --> 01:05:36,675
And she's telling you, you must get
Frig Hatun out of the tribe immediately.

702
01:05:38,345 --> 01:05:40,595
What are you talking about, Bayindir?

703
01:05:41,345 --> 01:05:46,725
This snake named Frig knows
everything we've done.

704
01:05:47,125 --> 01:05:50,365
- Am I right, Bengi Hatun?
- Yes indeed.

705
01:05:53,765 --> 01:05:56,235
You are right, but how?

706
01:05:56,305 --> 01:05:58,845
You need to figure that out.

707
01:05:59,335 --> 01:06:05,225
You never leave the tents. You gave your
daughter. You've become relatives.

708
01:06:06,115 --> 01:06:09,815
The difficult for us is easy for you.

709
01:06:10,465 --> 01:06:15,065
Mother Sultan has a ton of soldiers.
Why does she want our help?

710
01:06:18,345 --> 01:06:24,725
Ask this question to her yourself
if you're brave enough.

711
01:06:27,145 --> 01:06:28,805
Resolve this matter immediately.

712
01:06:31,715 --> 01:06:33,105
Bayindir.

713
01:06:36,485 --> 01:06:38,375
That's not going to happen.

714
01:06:38,375 --> 01:06:40,665
So, you're saying you can't,
huh Oktem?

715
01:06:42,065 --> 01:06:44,615
-Yes
-Well

716
01:06:45,785 --> 01:06:47,735
So, things will change.

717
01:06:54,385 --> 01:06:56,685
Mother Sultan sent this.

718
01:06:59,755 --> 01:07:07,385
And she said, if you can't get her out alive,
shut her up and stop her breathing.

719
01:07:18,835 --> 01:07:23,285
We will do that,
we have no other choice.

720
01:07:24,575 --> 01:07:26,105
Mother.

721
01:07:32,375 --> 01:07:33,945
I need to leave.

722
01:07:42,875 --> 01:07:45,225
Why did Bayindir Bey come?

723
01:07:46,415 --> 01:07:49,585
He's just messing around, bothering us.
Don't you know Bayindir?

724
01:07:54,615 --> 01:07:59,305
We're going to the tents tomorrow.
Prepare yourself quickly, come on

725
01:08:03,615 --> 01:08:06,695
This is your secret then, Osman

726
01:08:07,065 --> 01:08:11,865
We forge a relationship with
God through shamans.

727
01:08:13,965 --> 01:08:17,154
And you do it through your sheikh.

728
01:08:19,354 --> 01:08:26,274
We don't need a person to
bond with our Creator, Nayman

729
01:08:29,175 --> 01:08:34,259
Every person who believes in
Allah and His Messenger knows that...

730
01:08:34,259 --> 01:08:38,479
....their Lord is closer to them
than their jugular vein.

731
01:08:38,734 --> 01:08:41,404
What does this mean?

732
01:08:42,925 --> 01:08:51,734
This means our Creator knows each one of us,
that He is all-knowing.

733
01:08:53,285 --> 01:08:56,104
He knows every step we take.

734
01:08:57,734 --> 01:09:04,255
God is great. Not every person
can reach Him. Not whenever they want.

735
01:09:05,135 --> 01:09:09,245
But I don't understand your religion at all.

736
01:09:10,585 --> 01:09:16,444
Whenever Nayman encounters a Muslim
and draws his sword against him...

737
01:09:17,955 --> 01:09:21,245
He always hears the call of
Allahu Akbar(Allah is the greatest)

738
01:09:21,245 --> 01:09:23,194
I heard it, of course.

739
01:09:25,654 --> 01:09:28,694
And I buried many of them, Osman.

740
01:09:32,725 --> 01:09:35,265
Go on, Edebali.

741
01:09:36,125 --> 01:09:41,165
Those who fall as martyrs fall for the
sake of Allah, the Most High, the Great

742
01:09:43,225 --> 01:09:48,694
His mercy is wide, his wrath is frightening.

743
01:09:52,175 --> 01:09:59,245
And if people saw His torment in this world,
they would submit to his greatness.

744
01:10:00,425 --> 01:10:04,275
And their eyes would overflow
with tears like a river.

745
01:10:05,555 --> 01:10:10,345
Fortunetaly, His mercy reaches everyone
who asks for it.

746
01:10:11,215 --> 01:10:15,915
But if His people didn't
get to reach him...

747
01:10:16,505 --> 01:10:23,685
...people would say "O Lord! You didn't
let me reach you...

748
01:10:24,295 --> 01:10:26,675
...why are you holding me responsible?"

749
01:10:27,725 --> 01:10:33,125
I cannot call it God
if everyone talks to Him.

750
01:10:33,705 --> 01:10:36,775
I am a special servant of God's.

751
01:10:37,255 --> 01:10:40,805
And I am the image of his anger, Edebali.

752
01:10:47,155 --> 01:10:50,465
That's the difference between us, Commander.

753
01:10:51,485 --> 01:11:00,225
We fear the wrath of our Lord and have mercy
on the creature for the sake of the Creator.

754
01:11:01,865 --> 01:11:05,275
But you know nothing but tyranny.

755
01:11:06,875 --> 01:11:16,435
You hide your weakness under the name of mercy
and your fear under the name of your religion

756
01:11:17,105 --> 01:11:18,675
Don't hide.

757
01:11:20,585 --> 01:11:23,425
We never hide from anyone.

758
01:11:23,745 --> 01:11:29,765
Our religion commands us to
fight against the infidels until death.

759
01:11:30,895 --> 01:11:35,815
It commands us to raise the sword
until the whole world is right.

760
01:11:37,455 --> 01:11:40,205
We show mercy to the oppressed.

761
01:11:40,205 --> 01:11:44,265
And we only make peace with
the chivalrous enemies.

762
01:11:45,155 --> 01:11:48,385
So tell me, are you a chivalrous enemy?

763
01:11:49,265 --> 01:11:53,795
I am the most chivalrous enemy
you'll ever see, Osman.

764
01:11:58,735 --> 01:12:03,035
What do we do with
the chivalrous enemy, my sheikh?

765
01:12:03,645 --> 01:12:07,745
We inform them first.

766
01:12:11,155 --> 01:12:12,695
Listen.

767
01:12:14,425 --> 01:12:26,995
Those are who dispute Allah’s signs
with no proof given to them.

768
01:12:28,605 --> 01:12:34,525
How despicable is that for Allah and the believers!

769
01:12:37,805 --> 01:12:43,865
This is how Allah seals the heart of every arrogant tyrant.”
(Surah Ghafir - 35)

770
01:12:47,605 --> 01:12:49,875
Don't be so arrogant, Nayman.

771
01:12:50,715 --> 01:12:53,715
I invite you to Islam.

772
01:12:58,115 --> 01:13:03,035
Come and be honored by the grace of Islam.

773
01:13:05,215 --> 01:13:13,265
Now that you come and
eat and drink with us...

774
01:13:13,995 --> 01:13:17,715
...trust our pure intention
towards you.

775
01:13:19,640 --> 01:13:23,020
And if you are going to raise your sword,
raise it for Allah's sake

776
01:13:24,840 --> 01:13:27,370
And pronounce the shahada.

777
01:13:34,640 --> 01:13:37,420
Where did this come from?

778
01:13:40,650 --> 01:13:42,360
Why would I even do that?

779
01:13:46,850 --> 01:13:49,230
We have explained the truth to you.

780
01:13:50,390 --> 01:13:54,900
If you listen to us and believe,
you will be a faithful brother to us.

781
01:13:55,180 --> 01:14:03,710
If you turn away from and stay as an enemy,
our sword will always be against you.

782
01:14:05,380 --> 01:14:10,760
We, as our God commanded, show mercy
for those who deserves mercy...

783
01:14:10,760 --> 01:14:14,110
...and punish
those who deserves punishment.

784
01:14:26,450 --> 01:14:29,690
I'm tired of your words, Sheikh Edebali.

785
01:14:31,380 --> 01:14:41,400
There is a magic that I cannot understand,
but I will not submit to this magic.

786
01:14:41,490 --> 01:14:44,150
I will go now and rest.

787
01:14:48,130 --> 01:14:51,040
In the name of Allah,
the most gracious, the most merciful

788
01:15:10,175 --> 01:15:12,195
Nayman is in the tents.

789
01:15:13,865 --> 01:15:17,855
Osman Bey says there is no problem,
but we still have to be ready.

790
01:15:18,325 --> 01:15:24,560
We should, Konur brother, we should, but we
don't know what kind of an enemy Nayman is.

791
01:15:27,405 --> 01:15:31,220
Nayman walked into the military headquarters
they had set up on his own...

792
01:15:31,690 --> 01:15:35,080
...and said what he had to say to
Ismahan and the Beys.

793
01:15:35,285 --> 01:15:37,105
Hhe took what he wanted.

794
01:15:38,615 --> 01:15:39,855
What did he take?

795
01:15:41,905 --> 01:15:43,405
He took their courage away.

796
01:15:44,905 --> 01:15:49,465
And he came here with a few of his men
without worrying about his life.

797
01:15:49,535 --> 01:15:54,405
Nayman is different from the others.
He thinks differently from them.

798
01:15:56,225 --> 01:16:00,225
If he was like others, he would have come here
with his army and demonstrated his powers.

799
01:16:02,215 --> 01:16:05,815
Nayman wants to tell us that he am strong
even if his army is not with him.

800
01:16:05,815 --> 01:16:09,365
What happened, Gurbuz Alp?

801
01:16:10,175 --> 01:16:15,135
-I feel sad for Aktemur Bey.
-Why do you, Gurbuz?

802
01:16:16,375 --> 01:16:21,035
Our concern is one, but yours is two.

803
01:16:22,165 --> 01:16:24,015
You are getting married.

804
01:16:28,675 --> 01:16:32,855
We have had marriage ceremonies during wars
in the past, don't worry.

805
01:16:33,215 --> 01:16:41,535
I'm not talking about that, Aktemur Bey.
You'll understand after the marriage.

806
01:16:43,715 --> 01:16:47,595
Gurbuz, say what you want to say.

807
01:16:47,835 --> 01:16:51,545
Bengi Hatun will be your mother in law,
that's enough.

808
01:16:51,985 --> 01:16:53,795
What a pity.

809
01:16:56,775 --> 01:17:00,755
I hope Alcicek isn't like her mother.

810
01:17:03,935 --> 01:17:08,745
A brave man may win in the battleground,
but he loses to his wife at home.

811
01:17:09,525 --> 01:17:12,345
This shall be the only loss
Aktemur Bey gets.

812
01:17:14,725 --> 01:17:16,015
Thank you.

813
01:17:47,215 --> 01:17:51,985
Our Lord is great, and we say, Allah is the greatest.

814
01:17:55,045 --> 01:18:00,285
Those who fall as martyrs fall for the
sake of Allah, the Most High, the Great

815
01:18:02,575 --> 01:18:04,165
His mercy is wide.

816
01:18:07,365 --> 01:18:09,825
And his torment is frightenening.

817
01:18:12,705 --> 01:18:18,225
And if people saw His torment in this world,
they would submit to his greatness.

818
01:18:21,095 --> 01:18:26,255
Fortunetaly, His mercy reaches everyone
who asks for it.

819
01:18:27,775 --> 01:18:31,135
And that's the difference
between us, Commander.

820
01:18:31,985 --> 01:18:42,205
We fear the wrath of our Lord and have mercy
on the creature for the sake of the Creator

821
01:18:42,925 --> 01:18:46,715
But you know nothing but tyranny.

822
01:18:47,475 --> 01:18:49,815
Don't be so arrogant, Nayman.

823
01:18:50,385 --> 01:18:53,055
I invite you to Islam.

824
01:18:54,765 --> 01:18:58,345
Come and be honored by the grace of Islam.

825
01:19:06,765 --> 01:19:08,195
Malhun.

826
01:19:16,615 --> 01:19:19,645
- Malhun.
- My Osman.

827
01:19:20,165 --> 01:19:22,485
When did you come? I didn't hear you.

828
01:19:24,905 --> 01:19:31,115
I saw that you lost yourself.
You seem to be thinking of Orhan.

829
01:19:32,885 --> 01:19:36,795
He's starting to feel his legs.
The medicine is working.

830
01:19:37,195 --> 01:19:41,225
Of course it is, don't worry.

831
01:19:42,545 --> 01:19:44,875
Come on, put a smile on your face.

832
01:19:45,925 --> 01:19:49,375
It's not in my hands, my dear Osman,
my heart hurts.

833
01:19:50,355 --> 01:19:51,835
Yes, I know.

834
01:19:54,375 --> 01:19:56,755
I know the feeling.
I have the same.

835
01:19:57,385 --> 01:20:05,495
Now that we face this difficulty,
we will hold on to patience.

836
01:20:07,435 --> 01:20:11,295
I know that, my dear Osman...
and I say it to myself all the time, but I...

837
01:20:13,845 --> 01:20:19,775
I can't look Orhan's face
so he doesn't see fear in my eyes.

838
01:20:21,615 --> 01:20:23,745
I'm so tired.

839
01:20:28,105 --> 01:20:35,165
This pain pierced your,
but you endured and did not complain.

840
01:20:37,435 --> 01:20:41,795
You never showed your pain to anyone,
but I see it.

841
01:20:42,305 --> 01:20:45,435
You should rest now.
You'll rest.

842
01:20:48,415 --> 01:20:54,695
While you stand in the face of the whole world,
it is difficult for me to rest.

843
01:20:55,795 --> 01:21:02,315
But if I stay in this position for a while,
I will have gotten all the rest I need.

844
01:21:09,775 --> 01:21:14,135
You will rest until you can stand tall.

845
01:21:15,555 --> 01:21:20,265
I, our son, and our tribe need you.

846
01:21:24,865 --> 01:21:28,455
Nayman is getting ready to
raid our lands.

847
01:21:30,095 --> 01:21:35,155
I get my strength from you.
Our son gets his strength from you too.

848
01:21:37,255 --> 01:21:38,585
Malhun.

849
01:21:45,825 --> 01:21:50,925
Smile. Smile so that both
Orhan and our state shall rise.

850
01:23:01,055 --> 01:23:03,585
If you strike iron, it becomes a sword.

851
01:23:07,145 --> 01:23:10,635
And the man is like iron.

852
01:23:12,825 --> 01:23:15,725
You beat it, you crush it.

853
01:23:17,945 --> 01:23:23,925
It becomes a sword that sheds blood
and kills.

854
01:23:25,255 --> 01:23:29,915
Beys of this land are made of iron.

855
01:23:31,365 --> 01:23:34,065
We'll beat them first.

856
01:23:34,745 --> 01:23:37,105
Then we will praise them.

857
01:23:38,905 --> 01:23:40,835
And we will reward them.

858
01:23:41,135 --> 01:23:43,675
We will give them power.

859
01:23:44,465 --> 01:23:47,335
Only then will they show their loyalty.

860
01:23:48,085 --> 01:23:50,285
And they will be our dogs.

861
01:23:55,935 --> 01:23:57,885
Where's Commander Nayman?

862
01:23:58,045 --> 01:24:00,745
At the smelter, my Bey,
beating the iron.

863
01:24:06,995 --> 01:24:08,395
Osman.

864
01:24:12,195 --> 01:24:15,385
Osman, Osman.

865
01:24:16,645 --> 01:24:20,695
Osman is like iron.

866
01:24:21,575 --> 01:24:25,605
Don't you hear?

867
01:24:28,905 --> 01:24:33,905
Osman is a tree, a great tree.

868
01:24:35,745 --> 01:24:41,955
If you break him, he will dry,
and if you burn him, he will burn.

869
01:24:44,765 --> 01:24:46,905
If he burns...

870
01:24:49,465 --> 01:24:51,855
He's going to burn us all.

871
01:24:53,155 --> 01:24:55,655
What are you going to do, Mighty Nayman.

872
01:24:56,375 --> 01:24:59,765
I'll root him out.

873
01:25:00,345 --> 01:25:04,765
I will kill Osman.

874
01:25:06,185 --> 01:25:10,685
If he lives, I can't make anyone mankurt.

875
01:25:11,065 --> 01:25:14,865
Osman will die today.

876
01:25:43,145 --> 01:25:48,805
A man is like a sword,
if he remains motionless, he will rust, Osman.

877
01:25:54,765 --> 01:25:58,955
I dedicate this sword to your son.

878
01:25:59,385 --> 01:26:01,875
To use it when he regains his health.

879
01:26:11,395 --> 01:26:13,175
Thank you.

880
01:26:15,955 --> 01:26:17,665
Thank you.

881
01:26:19,985 --> 01:26:27,185
I am here until I die, Osman.

882
01:26:28,465 --> 01:26:31,755
Think of yourself.

883
01:27:03,445 --> 01:27:07,655
I will gather the Beys in Sogut.

884
01:27:07,835 --> 01:27:12,015
And you will come too,
and your gold will come.

885
01:27:13,295 --> 01:27:16,065
I'll be there, Commander Nayman.

886
01:27:17,505 --> 01:27:19,525
I will be there

887
01:27:41,615 --> 01:27:43,525
Orhan will recover.

888
01:27:43,665 --> 01:27:45,265
Thank Allah.

889
01:27:45,485 --> 01:27:48,885
They found the antidote,
thank Allah very much

890
01:27:49,245 --> 01:27:51,025
Thank Allah.

891
01:27:53,155 --> 01:27:55,925
This means that snake has spoken.

892
01:27:56,175 --> 01:27:59,735
She hasn't spoken yet but
we don't need her anymore.

893
01:28:00,085 --> 01:28:04,015
The only reason
she is still alive is because...

894
01:28:04,015 --> 01:28:08,765
she will tell the whole world about
her actions and her partners in crime

895
01:28:08,765 --> 01:28:11,875
I'll make her talk and I'll kill her in the field.

896
01:28:14,455 --> 01:28:17,785
Who found the antidote? Was it Kumral Abdal?

897
01:28:17,905 --> 01:28:19,185
Nayman.

898
01:28:20,015 --> 01:28:23,005
Nayman's healer brough the cure.

899
01:28:24,625 --> 01:28:29,395
Good, good, only Allah
knows who has the cure.

900
01:28:29,645 --> 01:28:32,185
He shall recover fast I hope.

901
01:28:32,565 --> 01:28:34,205
Hopefully.

902
01:28:35,425 --> 01:28:39,205
I want to ask something, can I?

903
01:28:39,565 --> 01:28:40,895
Go ahead.

904
01:28:41,495 --> 01:28:45,705
I also want to take out my rage on Frig.

905
01:28:45,905 --> 01:28:49,125
My brother's blood is still on her hands.

906
01:28:49,915 --> 01:28:54,945
You should have taken revenge on Olof,
whom you brought into the castle, Bengi Hatun.

907
01:28:55,465 --> 01:28:58,775
I wasn't aware of that, Bala Hatun.

908
01:28:59,535 --> 01:29:03,475
I would kill him today
if he faced me again.

909
01:29:05,925 --> 01:29:08,195
Enter.

910
01:29:10,805 --> 01:29:12,745
Let's enter.

911
01:29:13,165 --> 01:29:18,075
Let us take revenge on her for those days when
she used to laugh at us and then play games against us.

912
01:29:34,625 --> 01:29:36,315
You snake!

913
01:29:37,715 --> 01:29:42,005
Which face are you wearing now?

914
01:29:42,475 --> 01:29:44,595
Do you have another face?

915
01:29:44,905 --> 01:29:47,135
You will be punished for what you did!

916
01:29:51,275 --> 01:29:52,625
Bengi.

917
01:29:54,425 --> 01:29:58,725
You will meet your brother very soon.

918
01:29:59,085 --> 01:30:01,715
Olof will kill you all.

919
01:30:03,015 --> 01:30:05,555
Don't make a sound, I'll save you.

920
01:30:05,645 --> 01:30:08,165
Calm down, Bengi Hatun.

921
01:30:08,345 --> 01:30:10,015
We need her.

922
01:30:10,215 --> 01:30:12,085
Wait, mother.

923
01:30:12,305 --> 01:30:13,725
What are you doing?

924
01:30:13,905 --> 01:30:15,275
I will kill you!

925
01:30:15,415 --> 01:30:17,185
Don't you, Bengi Hatun!

926
01:30:17,395 --> 01:30:19,715
I will not leave my brother's blood
on the floor.

927
01:30:19,715 --> 01:30:21,675
Get Bengi Hatun out, Ayse.

928
01:30:21,675 --> 01:30:22,755
Come on.

929
01:30:24,585 --> 01:30:26,635
Wait for it, Frig.

930
01:30:26,795 --> 01:30:28,545
Your end will come.

931
01:30:29,205 --> 01:30:32,075
You will drown in the blood of the innocent
whose blood you shed.

932
01:30:44,745 --> 01:30:46,565
These are your last days, Frig.

933
01:30:47,305 --> 01:30:52,095
Very soon I will make you confess
in front of the people and I will kill you.

934
01:30:55,095 --> 01:31:01,005
You'll be the first to die
after I get out of here, Bala.

935
01:31:01,525 --> 01:31:05,465
I will sacrifice your blood for the great Odin.

936
01:31:08,795 --> 01:31:10,515
Shut up.

937
01:31:18,650 --> 01:31:20,430
Speak, Konur.

938
01:31:20,860 --> 01:31:24,750
We prepared the map, my Bey,
we located the gold.

939
01:31:25,800 --> 01:31:27,820
This is Candar's way.

940
01:31:28,950 --> 01:31:32,240
And this way leads to Karasi.

941
01:31:33,000 --> 01:31:35,680
And Germiyan will use this
way to carry his gold.

942
01:31:38,670 --> 01:31:44,020
Shall we attack each of these three convoys
that will carry gold, my Bey?

943
01:31:47,420 --> 01:31:48,700
No

944
01:31:50,860 --> 01:31:54,460
The road that leads to the Garmiyan
is the long way.

945
01:31:55,180 --> 01:31:57,500
This is the short way.

946
01:31:57,770 --> 01:32:01,010
The other way are different paths.

947
01:32:02,760 --> 01:32:08,160
So, they wish to unite the gold
before the gold reaches Sogut.

948
01:32:09,690 --> 01:32:15,000
The yellow corridor is where they will do it.

949
01:32:17,250 --> 01:32:18,530
Konur.

950
01:32:20,150 --> 01:32:21,770
You will go there.

951
01:32:22,080 --> 01:32:25,710
And you will attack them and
take their gold.

952
01:32:26,540 --> 01:32:27,890
As you command, my Bey.

953
01:32:28,050 --> 01:32:30,640
We know how cruel
the Mongols are, Osman Bey.

954
01:32:30,720 --> 01:32:35,240
When Nayman doesn't get the gold,
he will take it on his people.

955
01:32:35,470 --> 01:32:38,800
It wouldn't be worse than him
getting the gold.

956
01:32:43,950 --> 01:32:46,470
Neiman weighed us first.

957
01:32:47,620 --> 01:32:52,500
He knows that I am at the head of
the army that will defeat him.

958
01:32:53,620 --> 01:32:58,530
Because of this, he will want to kill me
after he takes the gold.

959
01:32:58,840 --> 01:33:03,540
He will prevent the resistance
and frighten the Beys.

960
01:33:04,820 --> 01:33:09,680
That gold will never reach him,
and nothing bad will happen to you.

961
01:33:10,400 --> 01:33:12,130
Well, what about Olof?

962
01:33:12,360 --> 01:33:15,930
...I will kill his patrols and
burn his convoys, but...

963
01:33:16,410 --> 01:33:18,950
Isn't it time, Osman Bey?

964
01:33:19,180 --> 01:33:22,180
When are we going to knock down
Ingol on Olof's head?

965
01:33:23,020 --> 01:33:28,070
Having Frig on our hands
will stop Olof for a while.

966
01:33:29,070 --> 01:33:33,110
But Neiman, Neiman can have him
under his control.

967
01:33:36,050 --> 01:33:39,920
If Olof entered under
Neiman's command...

968
01:33:40,100 --> 01:33:44,150
as Beys disengaged their armies,
we'll be stuck between them.

969
01:33:44,190 --> 01:33:45,780
We will prevent this.

970
01:33:47,110 --> 01:33:50,120
Olof will hear about Frig leaving the tribe.

971
01:33:50,550 --> 01:33:56,130
And then, when he also comes out,
Turgut Bey will attack him.

972
01:33:56,270 --> 01:33:59,400
My heart cannot bear the agony of my country
under the feet of the infidels.

973
01:33:59,600 --> 01:34:02,410
- This will be over, Osman Bey.
- Thank you.

974
01:34:03,420 --> 01:34:04,980
Malhun.

975
01:34:05,770 --> 01:34:11,100
Mother Sultan is confused,
and their armies are divided all over.

976
01:34:11,340 --> 01:34:15,500
We will take advantage of this
opportunity and get Yenisehir back.

977
01:34:15,510 --> 01:34:17,300
Certainly, my Bey.

978
01:34:17,380 --> 01:34:19,250
Bala is making the preparations.

979
01:34:19,340 --> 01:34:22,570
We will take back Yenişehir with one attack.

980
01:34:22,720 --> 01:34:24,220
Hopefully.

981
01:34:27,360 --> 01:34:30,480
And I'll take part in the meeting
that Nayman's having

982
01:34:31,700 --> 01:34:34,260
He wants to cut my throat.

983
01:34:34,620 --> 01:34:37,140
But I will cut his.

984
01:34:39,950 --> 01:34:43,330
The only thing that can save him
from my sword...

985
01:34:44,500 --> 01:34:46,700
...is that if he accepts Islam.

986
01:34:50,950 --> 01:34:53,580
Everyone go back to your work.

987
01:35:25,485 --> 01:35:31,535
Speak, Shaman.
You vomited the thing that wormed you.

988
01:35:38,385 --> 01:35:41,410
We didn't cut off the head of Osman...

989
01:35:42,600 --> 01:35:47,670
...the rebel who shed Sarul's blood, and cut
off the head of the messenger we sent.

990
01:35:50,175 --> 01:35:52,425
We sat at his table.

991
01:35:53,385 --> 01:35:55,955
We helped his son recover.

992
01:35:56,785 --> 01:35:59,715
If we don't throw his dead body
in front of his Beys now...

993
01:36:00,945 --> 01:36:07,605
You forgot how things work on earth while
getting in touch with the spirits too much!

994
01:36:11,095 --> 01:36:13,005
This is politics.

995
01:36:13,295 --> 01:36:16,535
I weighed him, I got to know him.

996
01:36:17,005 --> 01:36:20,745
I will cut off his head now.

997
01:36:22,925 --> 01:36:29,355
They will fear and the heavy taxes
will break their backs.

998
01:36:29,715 --> 01:36:34,535
They will kneel in front of me
and enter under my command.

999
01:36:34,715 --> 01:36:36,805
Exactly as I wanted.

1000
01:36:40,065 --> 01:36:42,605
What if they don't pay taxes?

1001
01:36:43,685 --> 01:36:45,265
They will.

1002
01:36:46,075 --> 01:36:52,115
I will have the most valuable thing
Beys know.

1003
01:36:52,795 --> 01:36:56,575
If they don't pay the taxes I want...

1004
01:36:56,715 --> 01:36:59,795
I will erase their souls.

1005
01:37:04,335 --> 01:37:05,865
Goktalay.

1006
01:37:07,415 --> 01:37:09,485
This is your mission.

1007
01:37:31,895 --> 01:37:33,615
Bengi Hatun.

1008
01:37:35,555 --> 01:37:39,835
What is this about, Bengi Hatun?
Didn't you say we would stop?

1009
01:37:40,075 --> 01:37:42,325
Shut up, Esma, shut up.

1010
01:37:42,665 --> 01:37:46,045
You're the one who got me into this,
shut up now.

1011
01:37:47,185 --> 01:37:48,915
Mother Sultan ordered.

1012
01:37:49,525 --> 01:37:51,305
Frig will die.

1013
01:37:52,585 --> 01:37:54,115
I can't do it.

1014
01:37:54,725 --> 01:37:57,495
Rejoice, for you will kill that infidel, Esma.

1015
01:37:58,235 --> 01:38:01,495
Her hands are stained with the blood
of many innocent people.

1016
01:38:03,005 --> 01:38:05,375
Frig will die.

1017
01:38:06,245 --> 01:38:09,765
If she stays alive and talks,
we're all done.

1018
01:38:10,585 --> 01:38:12,125
Move.

1019
01:38:13,285 --> 01:38:14,615
Come on.

1020
01:38:17,825 --> 01:38:19,735
Let her eat that and die!

1021
01:38:21,735 --> 01:38:23,355
Come on, Esma.

1022
01:38:32,465 --> 01:38:35,395
Inegol Castle

1023
01:38:36,205 --> 01:38:41,755
What about the cruelty?
The fact that I skinned...

1024
01:38:42,365 --> 01:38:44,455
...the people I killed.

1025
01:38:45,115 --> 01:38:47,335
Cutting their ears.

1026
01:38:49,745 --> 01:38:51,995
Cutting their heads.

1027
01:38:52,425 --> 01:38:54,765
How is it stated in our religion?

1028
01:38:56,025 --> 01:38:57,725
It is brutality.

1029
01:38:58,535 --> 01:39:07,035
But the Muslim, the Muslim
are the infidels.

1030
01:39:07,655 --> 01:39:09,965
They must be punished.

1031
01:39:10,195 --> 01:39:12,715
Don't worry, nun.

1032
01:39:13,405 --> 01:39:16,945
I will make them taste the pain
they have never tasted before

1033
01:39:19,815 --> 01:39:27,015
The Muslim blood you shed
will get you into heaven, Olof.

1034
01:39:28,475 --> 01:39:34,235
The great Jesus will sanctify you for the
services you render to the Christian cause.

1035
01:39:36,625 --> 01:39:38,145
Amen.

1036
01:39:38,645 --> 01:39:40,175
Amen.

1037
01:39:43,050 --> 01:39:44,755
What's going on?

1038
01:40:05,755 --> 01:40:07,305
Olof.

1039
01:40:25,885 --> 01:40:28,715
Is this your strength, Olof?

1040
01:40:37,155 --> 01:40:44,035
That's a pity, look at the man who was
entrusted with Andronicus' army!

1041
01:40:54,765 --> 01:40:58,615
Osman was talkable.
I talked to him.

1042
01:40:58,795 --> 01:41:02,775
You require sword, Olof.

1043
01:41:03,585 --> 01:41:08,125
I have to speak to you
in the language you understand.

1044
01:41:55,435 --> 01:41:57,995
You'll feed her, come on.

1045
01:42:26,265 --> 01:42:28,065
You will die if you don't eat.

1046
01:42:41,415 --> 01:42:43,485
So, stay hungry, it's no longer our fault

1047
01:42:43,715 --> 01:42:44,935
Come on, collect it

1048
01:43:45,565 --> 01:43:47,985
Welcome, Commander Nayman.

1049
01:43:49,665 --> 01:43:52,015
When you entered like that...

1050
01:43:52,335 --> 01:43:54,165
You pointed your sword at me.

1051
01:43:55,085 --> 01:43:57,165
I forgive you.

1052
01:43:57,165 --> 01:44:00,935
Otherwise, I would have watered
Inegol with your blood.

1053
01:44:02,985 --> 01:44:07,035
I have received your letter,
and your loyalty pleases me.

1054
01:44:07,565 --> 01:44:10,265
Because our destinies are similar.

1055
01:44:10,485 --> 01:44:12,665
You are lost in the chaos.

1056
01:44:12,665 --> 01:44:17,365
You can no longer even name
your children after you.

1057
01:44:18,235 --> 01:44:21,965
Genghis should have learned from you.

1058
01:44:22,435 --> 01:44:24,785
We are trying not to perish.

1059
01:44:26,085 --> 01:44:29,385
From now on, you'll only work for me.

1060
01:44:33,285 --> 01:44:35,715
I will do whatever it takes, Commander.

1061
01:44:37,615 --> 01:44:41,185
You'll wear out Osman.
You'll start with Turgut.

1062
01:44:41,685 --> 01:44:45,235
You will hit him at the first opportunity.

1063
01:44:46,085 --> 01:44:49,615
I will rip out Turgut's heart where I see him.

1064
01:44:50,015 --> 01:44:52,015
...I'll goug out his eyes.

1065
01:44:53,085 --> 01:44:57,465
Sister Irene. Get out.

1066
01:44:57,465 --> 01:44:59,465
You won't want to hear what I have to say.

1067
01:45:04,235 --> 01:45:05,435
Kam.

1068
01:45:07,035 --> 01:45:10,915
Give Olof a unit of Mongol soldiers.

1069
01:45:10,915 --> 01:45:13,615
They will swear allegiance to Olof.

1070
01:45:13,615 --> 01:45:15,615
And they will be under his command.

1071
01:45:18,535 --> 01:45:20,815
You were going to give me Frig.

1072
01:45:20,815 --> 01:45:23,565
I give you an army!

1073
01:45:23,765 --> 01:45:25,265
Isn't it enough?

1074
01:45:25,265 --> 01:45:27,265
That's enough, Commander.

1075
01:45:27,265 --> 01:45:29,815
But you were at Osman's table.

1076
01:45:29,815 --> 01:45:31,815
Not everyone at whose table I sit
is my friend.

1077
01:45:32,385 --> 01:45:36,815
And not everyone
whose table I destroy is my enemy.

1078
01:45:39,285 --> 01:45:41,315
Together, Commander.

1079
01:45:42,165 --> 01:45:44,685
We will destroy them together.

1080
01:45:53,465 --> 01:45:55,985
Don't fail, Olof.

1081
01:45:56,385 --> 01:45:58,485
I don't keep losers alive

1082
01:46:26,215 --> 01:46:27,715
Olof.

1083
01:46:32,165 --> 01:46:33,995
There's news on Frigg

1084
01:46:35,785 --> 01:46:40,365
They're relocating her because
we know she's in the Osman tribe

1085
01:46:42,715 --> 01:46:44,235
To where?

1086
01:46:44,235 --> 01:46:46,235
She is under Turgut's protection.

1087
01:46:46,465 --> 01:46:48,515
In Turgut tents.

1088
01:46:48,515 --> 01:46:50,515
Beautiful.

1089
01:46:51,165 --> 01:46:52,865
I'll take Frig.

1090
01:46:53,885 --> 01:46:56,785
I'll prove my sterngth to Nayman.

1091
01:46:56,785 --> 01:46:58,785
And he will see who I am.

1092
01:46:59,365 --> 01:47:03,835
Two corpses with one arrow.
Prepare our soldiers and the Mongol soldiers.

1093
01:47:03,835 --> 01:47:06,665
We'll go, come on.

1094
01:47:07,265 --> 01:47:08,565
Let's go.

1095
01:47:18,540 --> 01:47:20,270
Esma, did she eat?

1096
01:47:20,270 --> 01:47:21,790
She didn't.

1097
01:47:21,790 --> 01:47:24,370
She says she'd rather die to eat.

1098
01:47:26,940 --> 01:47:28,520
What do we do now?

1099
01:47:29,075 --> 01:47:32,105
There's no other way, I'll kill Frigg myself.

1100
01:47:35,455 --> 01:47:37,005
Bengi Hatun.

1101
01:47:38,975 --> 01:47:40,855
Hatuns brought the fabrics.

1102
01:47:44,475 --> 01:47:47,255
We chose, but come and
you take a look too.

1103
01:47:48,305 --> 01:47:50,075
It must be beautiful if you chose.

1104
01:47:50,705 --> 01:47:52,505
I just need Alcicek to love it.

1105
01:47:53,905 --> 01:47:58,055
They'll make the most beautiful
bridal dress for my Alcicek, right Ayse Hatun?

1106
01:47:58,055 --> 01:48:00,055
Of course, of course.

1107
01:48:00,055 --> 01:48:02,055
Everything fits on the beautiful.

1108
01:48:04,325 --> 01:48:06,125
Come on, let's go and see.

1109
01:48:11,425 --> 01:48:13,255
You are after something.

1110
01:48:13,825 --> 01:48:16,305
No, why would you say that?

1111
01:48:16,305 --> 01:48:18,305
It's over, Alcicek Hatun.

1112
01:48:32,325 --> 01:48:33,725
Cahit!

1113
01:48:35,075 --> 01:48:36,675
Abdullah!

1114
01:48:37,405 --> 01:48:38,675
Baykal!

1115
01:48:38,975 --> 01:48:40,125
Korkut!

1116
01:48:40,125 --> 01:48:42,125
Uyegil, come on.

1117
01:49:02,925 --> 01:49:05,425
They are coming, brother.

1118
01:49:05,525 --> 01:49:07,525
They are welcome to come.

1119
01:49:10,225 --> 01:49:12,955
What is going on here? Who are you?

1120
01:49:12,955 --> 01:49:14,825
Why do you block the way?

1121
01:49:15,575 --> 01:49:16,905
Turan.

1122
01:49:33,455 --> 01:49:34,775
Come on.

1123
01:49:34,775 --> 01:49:36,775
Come on, in the name of Allah.

1124
01:49:42,105 --> 01:49:44,955
We will not kill them,
it is enough that you arrest them.

1125
01:49:44,955 --> 01:49:46,955
Okay brother.

1126
01:50:17,975 --> 01:50:19,475
You tired us out!

1127
01:50:19,575 --> 01:50:21,575
We were about to kill you!

1128
01:50:27,975 --> 01:50:30,525
Our goal is not to kill you.

1129
01:50:33,605 --> 01:50:38,305
It's not.
And now the gold will go to its real owner.

1130
01:50:41,105 --> 01:50:43,975
You will be our guests for a while.

1131
01:51:00,240 --> 01:51:01,810
Cerkutay!

1132
01:51:02,060 --> 01:51:03,590
Cerkutay!

1133
01:51:05,240 --> 01:51:06,810
Come here.

1134
01:51:07,040 --> 01:51:09,590
Why are you screaming? They will hear now!

1135
01:51:09,590 --> 01:51:13,370
They'll set a trap, Olof will attack Turgut Bey,
what are we going to do now?

1136
01:51:13,370 --> 01:51:16,110
That Nayman or whatever his name is
gave him soldiers.

1137
01:51:16,610 --> 01:51:18,160
No way.

1138
01:51:18,460 --> 01:51:20,740
Turgut Bey had a plan.

1139
01:51:20,740 --> 01:51:23,110
But he must not have taken the Mongol
soldiers into account.

1140
01:51:24,260 --> 01:51:26,260
We have to inform him at once.

1141
01:51:29,460 --> 01:51:33,460
I pray that the Lord will surround
you with love in return for your services.

1142
01:51:33,460 --> 01:51:35,460
May goodness always be with you.

1143
01:51:38,640 --> 01:51:40,410
Sister Irene.

1144
01:51:42,190 --> 01:51:43,940
I was looking for you.

1145
01:51:44,390 --> 01:51:45,960
What's it?

1146
01:51:46,060 --> 01:51:51,290
I mean, the servants and I
were going to read the Bible.

1147
01:51:51,690 --> 01:51:54,410
We will start reading after
their work is done.

1148
01:51:55,060 --> 01:51:56,910
Read later.

1149
01:51:57,410 --> 01:51:59,240
Olof is waiting for you.

1150
01:51:59,960 --> 01:52:01,290
Of course.

1151
01:52:07,960 --> 01:52:10,090
Come on then, we can't keep him waiting.

1152
01:52:10,090 --> 01:52:12,090
Let's go.

1153
01:52:13,760 --> 01:52:15,510
Let's go, let's go.

1154
01:52:32,960 --> 01:52:34,290
Stop.

1155
01:52:38,095 --> 01:52:39,825
Turgut Bey.

1156
01:52:39,850 --> 01:52:41,650
I brought information from Cerkutay.

1157
01:52:41,650 --> 01:52:43,350
Come on, come on

1158
01:52:48,220 --> 01:52:49,570
- Turgut Bey.
- Tell me.

1159
01:52:49,570 --> 01:52:55,020
Nayman has given a unit of Mongol
soldiers to Olof to attack you.

1160
01:52:55,370 --> 01:52:57,170
They will set off soon.

1161
01:52:58,900 --> 01:53:00,700
Olof thinks he's a hunter.

1162
01:53:01,220 --> 01:53:03,250
But he will obviously become prey.

1163
01:53:05,570 --> 01:53:07,120
Thank you, Hristo

1164
01:53:07,770 --> 01:53:09,300
Thank you.

1165
01:53:11,050 --> 01:53:14,800
Now let's prepare a nice welcome
for that dishonorable dogs, alps!

1166
01:53:16,320 --> 01:53:18,900
Come on, my brave ones, come on

1167
01:53:22,240 --> 01:53:23,590
My Bey!

1168
01:53:28,700 --> 01:53:30,070
Talk.

1169
01:53:30,070 --> 01:53:32,320
My Bey, I brought information
from Konur Alp.

1170
01:53:32,320 --> 01:53:36,400
We captured the gold to go to Nayman.

1171
01:53:37,420 --> 01:53:38,920
Thank you.

1172
01:53:40,200 --> 01:53:41,720
Thank you.

1173
01:53:42,470 --> 01:53:44,250
Tell them to wait for my sign.

1174
01:53:44,250 --> 01:53:45,950
Your command, my Bey.

1175
01:54:01,085 --> 01:54:08,605
Hadrat Mother Sultan, as I mentioned before,
Frig Hatun is skillful.

1176
01:54:08,705 --> 01:54:10,705
She's not even eating.

1177
01:54:14,085 --> 01:54:17,415
If she speak, our relations with
Osman will be destroyed.

1178
01:54:18,615 --> 01:54:20,465
...it doesn't matter, however...

1179
01:54:21,435 --> 01:54:23,615
This is not the right time, Bayindir.

1180
01:54:24,965 --> 01:54:26,365
You understand this, right?

1181
01:54:29,315 --> 01:54:32,085
Frig should not speak.

1182
01:54:34,215 --> 01:54:36,735
She won't speak, Mother Sultan.

1183
01:54:36,735 --> 01:54:39,065
Never worry.

1184
01:54:39,615 --> 01:54:41,435
I will solve it.

1185
01:54:41,435 --> 01:54:44,835
If my name is Bayindir, son of Shunder

1186
01:54:45,315 --> 01:54:49,635
I will kill that snake called Frig with
her own venom.

1187
01:54:59,535 --> 01:55:02,135
Mother Sultan, Osman Bey arrived.

1188
01:55:07,725 --> 01:55:08,645
Let him.

1189
01:55:20,065 --> 01:55:21,435
Peace be upon you.

1190
01:55:21,435 --> 01:55:22,735
And may peace be upon you too.

1191
01:55:22,735 --> 01:55:24,735
Peace be upon you, Osman Bey.

1192
01:55:25,335 --> 01:55:26,915
You came early.

1193
01:55:26,915 --> 01:55:29,785
No, I came just in time.

1194
01:55:31,515 --> 01:55:34,685
Surely there's a reason I came before Nayman.

1195
01:55:40,835 --> 01:55:41,965
Where are the Beys?

1196
01:55:43,365 --> 01:55:46,285
The Beys have spent the night
at my palace in Yenişehir.

1197
01:55:46,285 --> 01:55:48,285
They should be on their way now.

1198
01:55:48,585 --> 01:55:52,165
You tell me, why did you come early?

1199
01:55:52,165 --> 01:55:54,165
No.

1200
01:55:54,865 --> 01:55:58,985
The palace and Yenişehir
are no longer yours.

1201
01:56:06,935 --> 01:56:09,515
Kayi banners are waving in Yenişehir.

1202
01:56:34,015 --> 01:56:36,365
O brave soldiers of the great Seljuk state!

1203
01:56:36,835 --> 01:56:38,785
We do not intend to kill you!

1204
01:56:39,535 --> 01:56:43,835
But the time has come for us
to take what belongs to us.

1205
01:56:48,635 --> 01:56:52,335
Now put down your swords
and leave Yenişehir.

1206
01:56:52,935 --> 01:56:58,515
Never! We will not leave this place until
an order comes from our Mother Sultan.

1207
01:57:00,585 --> 01:57:02,915
So, protect yourselves!

1208
01:57:04,535 --> 01:57:06,115
Aktemur.

1209
01:57:08,065 --> 01:57:10,465
No one will shed blood.

1210
01:57:10,465 --> 01:57:12,465
Arrest them.

1211
01:57:13,585 --> 01:57:14,885
Alps!

1212
01:57:14,885 --> 01:57:16,265
Sisters, let's go.

1213
01:58:14,285 --> 01:58:16,065
Turgut.

1214
01:58:16,075 --> 01:58:18,575
I came to kill you, Olof.

1215
01:58:19,425 --> 01:58:20,795
Shields!

1216
01:58:25,725 --> 01:58:27,595
Pull!

1217
01:58:35,395 --> 01:58:37,195
Pull!

1218
01:58:43,025 --> 01:58:46,025
Allah is the greatest!

1219
01:58:50,395 --> 01:58:52,275
Oh right!

1220
01:58:55,345 --> 01:58:56,845
Olof!

1221
01:58:58,495 --> 01:59:00,575
You don't have anywhere to escape.

1222
01:59:01,795 --> 01:59:06,145
And you don't have any solution anymore.
It's time for you to bow down.

1223
01:59:06,145 --> 01:59:08,145
Now it's time to finish you off.

1224
01:59:08,145 --> 01:59:10,145
You are the only one to...

1225
01:59:10,325 --> 01:59:12,145
...bow down, Turgut.

1226
01:59:12,145 --> 01:59:13,945
You will kneel!

1227
01:59:13,945 --> 01:59:15,945
We make the mighty kneel!

1228
01:59:16,475 --> 01:59:17,945
And we make the one with
the raised head bow his head!

1229
01:59:18,695 --> 01:59:21,975
No one dares to make Turks kneel!

1230
01:59:22,825 --> 01:59:24,595
And you will see this now!

1231
01:59:28,525 --> 01:59:31,045
Ulgen Hatun is among them, my Bey.

1232
01:59:34,925 --> 01:59:37,225
Protect the nun.

1233
01:59:38,325 --> 01:59:40,975
We will break their shields.

1234
01:59:41,545 --> 01:59:44,145
We will slam their bodies on the ground!

1235
01:59:45,725 --> 01:59:48,595
Allah is the greatest!

1236
01:59:51,025 --> 01:59:53,595
Stand still!

1237
01:59:54,125 --> 01:59:56,645
Allah is the greatest!

1238
01:59:57,095 --> 01:59:59,975
Get ready!

1239
02:00:47,745 --> 02:00:50,545
Withdraw!

1240
02:00:54,645 --> 02:00:56,145
Kutan!

1241
02:01:05,495 --> 02:01:08,025
Protect nun Irene!

1242
02:02:17,250 --> 02:02:20,149
Sogut

1243
02:02:44,745 --> 02:02:47,295
I offered you Yenişehir before.

1244
02:02:47,475 --> 02:02:49,345
But you didn't take it.

1245
02:02:51,395 --> 02:02:53,775
And now, under these
difficult circumstances...

1246
02:02:53,845 --> 02:02:56,485
And while Sogut is under Nayman's threat...

1247
02:02:56,505 --> 02:02:58,565
Don't drive me crazy, Osman!

1248
02:03:00,415 --> 02:03:04,035
Nayman will not only throw a feast in Sogut.

1249
02:03:05,045 --> 02:03:06,595
He will seize it.

1250
02:03:08,875 --> 02:03:10,375
open your eyes

1251
02:03:10,795 --> 02:03:13,325
This is not time to rebel!

1252
02:03:13,745 --> 02:03:15,455
We are at war.

1253
02:03:17,455 --> 02:03:21,675
Because of your mistake,
we begun with loss.

1254
02:03:24,365 --> 02:03:25,385
From now on...

1255
02:03:26,715 --> 02:03:28,245
I am on the field.

1256
02:03:29,895 --> 02:03:31,355
I am owning what's mine.

1257
02:03:39,415 --> 02:03:42,235
And you won't say anything about it.

1258
02:03:43,725 --> 02:03:44,805
Mother Sultan.

1259
02:03:46,665 --> 02:03:49,325
Osman Bey, you can't pay for this!

1260
02:03:49,895 --> 02:03:51,325
Today we should unite!

1261
02:03:53,605 --> 02:03:55,845
Let's get over with this Nayman trouble.

1262
02:03:57,805 --> 02:04:00,845
And then we'll talk, Mother Sultan.

1263
02:04:03,265 --> 02:04:04,855
Osman.

1264
02:04:17,685 --> 02:04:19,775
Mother Sultan, the Beys have arrived.

1265
02:04:22,775 --> 02:04:24,135
Let them.

1266
02:04:26,045 --> 02:04:27,415
Let them.

1267
02:04:28,805 --> 02:04:30,135
Let them.

1268
02:04:33,645 --> 02:04:35,435
Peace be upon you.

1269
02:04:37,245 --> 02:04:39,005
And may peace be upon you.

1270
02:04:43,585 --> 02:04:45,435
Welcome, Beys.

1271
02:04:46,345 --> 02:04:48,355
Thank you, mother Sultan.

1272
02:05:00,115 --> 02:05:02,235
The reign of Mother Sultan has ended here.

1273
02:05:03,165 --> 02:05:05,865
Alps, take the soldiers to Mother Sultan.

1274
02:05:06,405 --> 02:05:08,245
Their lives are entrusted to us.

1275
02:05:28,055 --> 02:05:30,645
Thank Allah.

1276
02:05:41,095 --> 02:05:42,855
Kutlu, Gokluce!

1277
02:05:43,415 --> 02:05:44,825
Raise our banner, come on

1278
02:06:22,205 --> 02:06:25,505
Thank Allah, we got our palace back.

1279
02:06:27,645 --> 02:06:29,615
What is ours will always be ours.

1280
02:06:30,855 --> 02:06:34,255
Every piece of land we took
with our blood and our souls...

1281
02:06:34,745 --> 02:06:37,525
...will remain ours forever,
if Lord allows.

1282
02:06:42,155 --> 02:06:43,545
Now its ours.

1283
02:06:44,225 --> 02:06:46,235
And after us, its our children's.

1284
02:06:47,015 --> 02:06:49,875
They will carry this banner to the whole world!

1285
02:06:50,255 --> 02:06:53,125
They will say the word of Allah,
make everyone hear.

1286
02:06:53,955 --> 02:06:57,305
Our aim is to uphold
the words of Allah.

1287
02:06:58,005 --> 02:07:00,055
We are going to bring order to the world.

1288
02:07:00,205 --> 02:07:02,415
Our seeds are in Kayi tents.

1289
02:07:02,825 --> 02:07:04,885
And we will sprout in Yenisehir.

1290
02:07:06,935 --> 02:07:10,785
And then our target will be the whole world!

1291
02:07:11,955 --> 02:07:15,275
Allah is the greatest!

1292
02:07:15,325 --> 02:07:18,145
Allah is the greatest!

1293
02:07:18,165 --> 02:07:21,205
Allah is the greatest!

1294
02:07:21,475 --> 02:07:26,045
Allah is the greatest!

1295
02:07:26,285 --> 02:07:28,285
When will this Nayman come?

1296
02:07:28,935 --> 02:07:31,955
You want your loss to be certain, Candar Bey?

1297
02:07:36,065 --> 02:07:38,415
Cut it out, Osman Bey!

1298
02:07:40,645 --> 02:07:42,215
You did a mistake.

1299
02:07:44,415 --> 02:07:45,985
With one mistake...

1300
02:07:46,465 --> 02:07:48,355
The penalty fell on our people.

1301
02:07:52,045 --> 02:07:53,085
Karasi Bey.

1302
02:07:55,835 --> 02:07:57,595
How many people struggled?

1303
02:07:58,015 --> 02:08:00,445
Just because you needed to
pay taxes to an cruel.

1304
02:08:01,045 --> 02:08:02,085
Tell me.

1305
02:08:03,945 --> 02:08:08,595
As if it's not you who
caused us this trouble!

1306
02:08:10,965 --> 02:08:12,995
The trouble has always been here.

1307
02:08:14,965 --> 02:08:16,845
I just ended it.

1308
02:08:22,035 --> 02:08:24,895
While you were being dogs
of Mother Sultan...

1309
02:08:27,865 --> 02:08:30,725
I killed the cruel in Konya.
Just because of that...

1310
02:08:31,665 --> 02:08:33,395
...you considered me an enemy.

1311
02:08:38,195 --> 02:08:40,055
Osman Bey is right.

1312
02:08:40,535 --> 02:08:42,845
If he hadn't done it, I would have done it.

1313
02:08:42,875 --> 02:08:44,095
It doesn't matter anymore.

1314
02:08:48,555 --> 02:08:51,545
What happened happened.
The price shall be paid, Osman Bey.

1315
02:08:52,455 --> 02:08:54,325
Gold will be here shortly.

1316
02:08:55,685 --> 02:08:56,705
Who knows?

1317
02:08:58,105 --> 02:08:59,935
Gold may never come.

1318
02:09:05,905 --> 02:09:07,735
Osman Bey, no way...

1319
02:09:08,855 --> 02:09:10,815
I have nothing to do with gold.

1320
02:09:12,825 --> 02:09:15,895
But of course I don't want
the gold to get to Nayman

1321
02:09:17,775 --> 02:09:19,665
If a price is to be paid...

1322
02:09:20,775 --> 02:09:22,585
...it shouldn't be paid with gold.

1323
02:09:23,395 --> 02:09:25,245
Rather, it must be paid with blood.

1324
02:09:26,635 --> 02:09:28,665
This is the only way to equalize.

1325
02:09:33,795 --> 02:09:35,555
Osman Bey

1326
02:09:36,185 --> 02:09:39,765
If you are related to gold issue...

1327
02:09:41,535 --> 02:09:46,075
And if even an alp of mine gets hurt
because of this...

1328
02:09:47,645 --> 02:09:49,485
You will pay dearly.

1329
02:09:52,225 --> 02:09:54,265
Because of the mistakes you made...

1330
02:09:55,835 --> 02:09:58,035
...we paid the highest price.

1331
02:10:04,575 --> 02:10:06,415
Now...

1332
02:10:13,685 --> 02:10:15,745
From now on, everything goes as I say.

1333
02:10:20,365 --> 02:10:22,485
The army will gather again.

1334
02:10:24,895 --> 02:10:26,745
And the head of this army....

1335
02:10:29,895 --> 02:10:31,615
...will be me.

1336
02:10:56,455 --> 02:10:58,185
Commander Nayman has come

1337
02:11:04,695 --> 02:11:06,065
Let him.

1338
02:11:26,840 --> 02:11:30,380
I did not see my gold in the
courtyard of the palace, Osman.

1339
02:11:38,920 --> 02:11:40,510
Beys.

1340
02:11:42,540 --> 02:11:44,100
Where is my gold?

1341
02:11:58,720 --> 02:12:00,150
Mother.

1342
02:12:18,040 --> 02:12:19,600
Where is my gold?

1343
02:12:53,630 --> 02:12:55,690
Where is my gold?

1344
02:13:38,280 --> 02:13:39,860
Kasim Bey.

1345
02:13:43,600 --> 02:13:45,190
What are you doing?

1346
02:13:53,830 --> 02:13:55,350
Soldiers!

1347
02:13:55,740 --> 02:13:57,770
Don't ignore this cruelty!

1348
02:14:08,100 --> 02:14:10,630
Kasim Bey, Yakup Bey's son.

1349
02:14:21,120 --> 02:14:23,680
Yusuf Bey, Candar Bey's son.

1350
02:14:31,840 --> 02:14:33,620
Yusuf Bey...

1351
02:14:34,220 --> 02:14:35,780
...Karasi Bey's son.

1352
02:15:02,800 --> 02:15:05,340
They're all prisoners of Commander Nayman

1353
02:15:06,690 --> 02:15:08,390
Get out of our way!

1354
02:15:09,720 --> 02:15:11,080
Or else...

1355
02:15:13,340 --> 02:15:16,100
We will tie you behind our horses.

1356
02:15:16,820 --> 02:15:19,580
And we will trample you under our horseshoes.

1357
02:15:21,570 --> 02:15:23,160
It is clear that...

1358
02:15:23,190 --> 02:15:25,780
Wolves are trying to strangle the lion...

1359
02:15:26,120 --> 02:15:28,210
...not being aware of their power.

1360
02:15:31,405 --> 02:15:33,925
Have you thought the end of this, Beys?

1361
02:15:35,245 --> 02:15:38,755
If you are in the den of wolves,
even if you are a lion...

1362
02:15:39,835 --> 02:15:41,565
...one wolf is enough for you.

1363
02:15:42,315 --> 02:15:44,845
Osman, do you have gold?

1364
02:15:46,315 --> 02:15:48,185
I have nothing to do with gold.

1365
02:15:49,325 --> 02:15:52,525
The gold is yours and you should be
the one who knows where it is.

1366
02:15:53,335 --> 02:15:54,635
Why do you ask me?

1367
02:15:56,985 --> 02:16:00,915
Do you think you can beat me?

1368
02:16:02,715 --> 02:16:05,965
You try to play with me...

1369
02:16:06,275 --> 02:16:09,275
But there is something you do not know.

1370
02:16:22,495 --> 02:16:25,885
You tried to bite me, huh?

1371
02:16:27,815 --> 02:16:31,375
You can't even snarl at me from now on!

1372
02:16:43,245 --> 02:16:44,605
Son!

1373
02:16:52,965 --> 02:16:54,665
Commander Nayman.

1374
02:16:58,485 --> 02:17:00,254
I will give you whatever you want.

1375
02:17:00,525 --> 02:17:02,365
Just don't hurt my son.

1376
02:17:05,895 --> 02:17:07,915
Son, my valiant!

1377
02:17:10,105 --> 02:17:11,695
The light of my eyes!

1378
02:17:19,025 --> 02:17:20,545
Do not!

1379
02:17:23,013 --> 02:17:25,815
Nothing is apparent yet!

1380
02:17:26,855 --> 02:17:30,725
Don't make us pay with our sons!

1381
02:17:35,115 --> 02:17:36,465
My valiant!

1382
02:17:45,125 --> 02:17:46,843
Commander Nayman

1383
02:17:47,433 --> 02:17:50,455
Kill me but let my son stay alive.

1384
02:17:51,334 --> 02:17:54,645
I'm doing nothing, Beys.

1385
02:17:55,785 --> 02:17:59,924
He who captured the gold is the same person
that is about to kill your sons.

1386
02:18:02,395 --> 02:18:07,275
You will pay the price of gold
with the lives of your children.

1387
02:18:09,135 --> 02:18:11,683
If you don't bring me gold...

1388
02:18:12,065 --> 02:18:13,924
...heads will fall.

1389
02:18:15,145 --> 02:18:16,995
And I think that...

1390
02:18:17,275 --> 02:18:20,825
The reason for all this is you, Osman.

1391
02:19:14,735 --> 02:19:18,763
Your courage will cause your captivity.

1392
02:19:24,555 --> 02:19:28,635
The blood of your children will be spilled in this khan

1393
02:20:03,185 --> 02:20:06,205
The price for my gold is this.

1394
02:20:31,515 --> 02:20:33,425
Stop now!

1395
02:20:34,125 --> 02:20:35,885
Stop!

1396
02:20:38,895 --> 02:20:41,755
Don't, Nayman.
Stop!

1397
02:20:48,475 --> 02:20:52,015
You are taking our children away
without confirming the guilty.

1398
02:20:53,015 --> 02:20:54,335
This is not the behavior of a man.

1399
02:20:55,065 --> 02:20:57,605
He who is born by the sword dies by the sword.

1400
02:20:57,635 --> 02:21:04,195
But Allah alone knows who will pay the price.

1401
02:21:27,385 --> 02:21:39,515
Visit our website for more: turkision.com